lass="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Upload what is asked, or write Your answer, and press <b class="gd-ui">Send my answer</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">We review it within 1 business day. Once we approve your application, you get an email and Home shows Check and sign.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">No typing the VIN: press <b class="gd-ui">Scan the barcode</b> and point your phone at the barcode in the driver&#39;s door frame or at the bottom of the windshield, or <b class="gd-ui">Photo of the VIN</b> and take a photo of it. Check the VIN shown before you continue.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Photos:</b> on your car&#39;s page, <b class="gd-ui">Add photos</b> takes any number at once, in any order. We sort them, put the outside photos on our studio background and touch up the inside ones. Photos that fit no shot go in with <b class="gd-ui">Extra outside photos</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Extra inside and detail photos</b>. At least 10 are needed.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="apply-and-get-your-car-listed-a-fleet-supplier-lease-your-cars-to-carmacars" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A fleet supplier: lease your cars to CarmaCars</h2><p class="gd-p">For a corporation that leases its cars to CarmaCars for a fixed amount a month. You pay CarmaCars no fees: no invoices, no debits.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Go to <span class="gd-url">carmacars.ca/list-your-car</span> and press <b class="gd-ui">A corporation with a fleet? Lease your cars to us as a fleet supplier</b> (or choose <b class="gd-ui">A corporation</b> in the application, then <b class="gd-ui">Fleet supplier: lease your cars to CarmaCars</b>).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">About you: the corporation&#39;s legal name and number, its registered address, and the signing officer&#39;s name and title.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">For each car: type the VIN (the year, make and model fill in), then the plate, and mark the car <b class="gd-ui">Regular</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Troubled</b> (it needs work). Each tier shows its lease a month. The tier is set when you add the car and does not change.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Say who the car is registered to now: <b class="gd-ui">My corporation</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Me or another officer, personally</b> (it moves into your corporation), or <b class="gd-ui">A seller: the corporation is buying it</b>. For the last two, enter the name and address on the ownership and the transfer or sale date.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Continue</b>, check the review and press <b class="gd-ui">Submit application</b>. The ServiceOntario forms each car needs are filled in for you at once, under <b class="gd-ui">Documents</b>: the lease to CarmaCars (CarmaCars holds the plates while it leases the car) and, for a car not yet registered to your corporation, the transfer into it. A seller signs the transfer on the back of the ownership. Only the empty boxes are filled. Sign each one on screen under <b class="gd-ui">Documents</b>, then print it and sign it in ink at ServiceOntario.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">In your owner portal, open <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b>, then each car, and upload its ownership (registration) copy.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">We check each car. Once we approve it, it is on the lease at its tier and Home shows <b class="gd-ui">Check and sign</b>: you sign the Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement, the Title-Holding and Lease Agreement and Form B (the lease summary) in the owner portal, on screen (there is no paper option). Form D (the limited power of attorney) is in your Documents too: you sign it on screen with two witnesses beside you, and CarmaCars signs its Part 2 at the same moment.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Home and <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> show <b class="gd-ui">Your fleet lease</b>: each car, its tier, its lease a month and the next payment date. The lease is paid on the 10th for the month before, with your statement; the first payment comes at least one full month after the car goes on the lease, and part months are paid by the day. Add more cars from your owner portal the same way.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="apply-and-get-your-car-listed-sign-first-then-cars" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Sign first, then cars</h2><p class="gd-p">You sign your agreement before any car comes over. As soon as your profile has your legal or corporation name, your address and, for a corporation, the signing officer and title, your agreement is made from it: the Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement (with the Title-Holding and Lease Agreement it relies on) if you lease cars to CarmaCars, the Vehicle Enrollment Agreement otherwise. No car is needed.</p><p class="gd-p">Your owner portal home shows six steps: Your profile, Sign the agreement, Add your cars, Photos and inspection, Approved, Delivered. The current step has one button; press it.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Sign the agreement.</b> Read and sign opens it, filled in from your profile. You sign once on screen; CarmaCars countersigns at the same moment.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Add your cars.</b> One at a time, or as a list of VINs from Cars &gt; Add cars from a VIN list (a fleet supplier gives each car its tier and plate there). Each car goes on Schedule A of your agreement as a numbered entry, and you confirm each batch with one signature (Confirm my cars). Its government forms are made at the same moment.</li><li>A car is approved, delivered or rented only once your agreement and its Schedule A entry are signed. If CarmaCars approved it before you signed, it goes through by itself the moment you sign.</li></ul><h3 class="gd-h3">Your car&#39;s steps, one at a time</h3><p class="gd-p">Once a car is on its way, Home shows <b class="gd-ui">Your next step</b> and each car&#39;s page shows <b class="gd-ui">Your car&#39;s steps</b>: every step of its onboarding, the one thing to do now with its button, what to bring, where to go and how long it takes. You are emailed and texted when a step is yours.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">The route.</b> <em>Transfer</em>: the car&#39;s registration moves into CarmaCars&#39; name. <em>Co-Registrant</em>: CarmaCars is added beside you. <em>Lease</em>: your corporation keeps the car and leases it to CarmaCars (no title transfer). An individual who leases through a new Owner Corporation first sets it up: Incorporate now opens our online incorporation partner (about 20 minutes), then upload the certificate.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">The steps.</b> Application, Terms approved, Agreements signed, Documents uploaded (your driver&#39;s licence, both sides of the ownership permit, your insurance slip and, if the car is financed, the lender&#39;s payout letter; a corporation gives its corporate documents), Ownership transfer, New registration uploaded, Plate and insurance on the fleet policy, Inspected and photographed, Listed.</li><li>Ownership transfer. Press <b class="gd-ui">Find a ServiceOntario centre</b>, book a time, then <b class="gd-ui">I booked it</b> with the time and the centre. Bring your licence, the original ownership permit, proof of insurance, the filled Form A and transfer documents (Documents &gt; Government forms), the Used Vehicle Information Package and the Safety Standards Certificate when the step lists them. You pay the registry&#39;s charges at the counter unless your Vehicle Schedule says CarmaCars pays them. After the counter, tick that the fees are paid and press <b class="gd-ui">Transfer done</b>, then upload the new ownership permit on the car&#39;s page.</li><li>A step that waits on CarmaCars says <b class="gd-ui">With CarmaCars</b>: nothing to do on your side.</li></ul></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'owners-and-onboarding', 'chapter', 'chauffeur-service', 'Owners apply on the site with List your car. Every application waits for you in one place, Applications: approve it, ask the owner for something, or decline it. Approved owners sign and pay in their portal.

## Applications

**People** > **Applications**. Every owner application, newest first.

1. The chips filter by status: New, Waiting on owner, Approved, Declined, or All. New applications also show on To do.
2. Each row shows the application number, the owner, the car, how many of the four checks are done, and when they applied.
3. Open an application to decide.

![](/guides/img/admin-33-applications-desktop-152f9e34.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 640; address: carmacars.ca/admin/applications; pins: 1 36.8 39.7, 2 48.6 53.1, 3 19.8 53.1")

## Decide on an application

One page holds everything: the owner, the car, the uploads, the four checks and the notes.

1. Check the driver''s licence, the ownership, the insurance and the lender or lessor. Mark each one Checked, fine, Problem or Not needed.
2. Press **Approve**. The step "Terms and first invoice" opens for each car, filled in with the owner''s negotiated terms (or the standard grid): Insurance Fee, Tracker Fee, management fee (Revenue Share), Install Fee and the first and last month amount (2 x the Insurance Fee unless you type an exact amount). Change any of them to the cent; with several cars, **Use these terms for every car** copies the first car''s numbers to the others.
3. Choose the invoices: First and last month, Registration fee (any exact amount), Tracker install (only once trackers are available) and Another invoice. For each one choose Send now, Save as draft or Already paid. Already paid asks how (e-Transfer, cash, cheque, bank transfer or other), the date and the reference: it is recorded like Record payment and the owner gets no email (no invoice, no receipt) unless you tick the receipt.
4. Press **Approve** at the bottom of the step. Nothing is set or sent before that. The owner becomes active, the documents open for one signature in their portal, only the invoices you chose are made, and the owner gets one email.
5. Missing something? Press **Ask for something**, tick what you need (for example the ownership permit or the insurance slip), add a message if you like, and press **Send to the owner**. The owner gets an email and a task in their portal; the application shows Waiting on owner until they answer.
6. Not a fit? Press **Decline**, write the Reason the owner reads, and press **Decline the application**. The owner is emailed for each car.

![](/guides/img/admin-34-application-desktop-98b64f92.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 812; address: carmacars.ca/admin/applications/c324ef8d-ad00-4bcc-bf04-ca68628a26b4; pins: 1 72.9 67.1, 2 73.9 42.9, 3 84.7 42.9, 4 72.9 49.6")

The application has an Invoices tab: every invoice of its cars, drafts and voids included. An application staff entered for the owner says "Entered by staff" and who; approving it sends the owner the set-up email (review the details and sign) instead of the approval email.

> Tip: Notes on the page are for staff only: **Add note** keeps a line on the record. When the owner answers a request, their answer is in the notes and the application is New again.

## Add a car for an owner

**People** > **Owners**, the **Add a car** tab, or **Add another car** on an owner''s page. The owner never has to fill in the application.

1. The owner: find them by name, email or phone, or choose New owner and enter the name, email, phone and address.
2. The car: press **Take a photo** (or **Choose a photo**) under Fill this from the ownership permit, and the plate, VIN, colour, permit number and plate sticker expiry fill in, with the year, make, model code and body read for you to check. Each detail shows Checked, Check this (for example a VIN that fails its check digit, a plate not in the usual format, or a sticker already expired) or Type it; the photo is attached as the ownership permit. Or type the VIN. The car is looked up at once and shown in one line (Edit if something is wrong); no VIN at hand, add it by its plate with the year, make and model from the lists. Tap the colour, check the class, then the odometer, insurer and whether it is owned, financed or leased. Photos are optional: the listing shows sample photos until real ones are added. Upload the ownership permit, the insurance slip and the lender''s information if you have them.
3. Terms and first invoice: the same fields as Approve. For another car of the same owner they start from that owner''s terms, or their other car''s; change them for this car.
4. Who sourced the owner: Entered for CarmaCars, or I sourced this owner (only then are you recorded as the one who brought the owner). The owner signs in the owner portal after one email (no paper signature).
5. Press **Add the car and set it up**. The owner gets one email: review the details, correct anything, and sign. An owner with no sign-in gets the link to choose a password in that same email.

Customer service and fleet assistants add cars the same way from their portal; theirs wait in Applications for you, with the terms and invoices they proposed already filled in. On an approved application staff entered, **Send the set-up email again** sends the owner the email with a fresh link.

## Owners

**People** > **Owners**. Every owner, with their cars and where onboarding stands.

1. Each owner shows their application, how many cars, and where onboarding stands.
2. **View as (owner portal)** shows their portal. **Send password link** helps them sign in.
3. Invite an owner on file: fill in Name and Email under Invite an owner, then press **Send invitation**.

![](/guides/img/admin-12-owners-desktop-3a54d505.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 560; address: carmacars.ca/admin/owners; pins: 1 41.0 42.9, 2 37.4 49.3, 3 77.4 82.5")

The owner signs everything at once in their portal (Check and sign: the agreements, schedules and Forms A and B; the official registry forms are printed and signed in ink). The confirmations to tick, then one signature: CarmaCars countersigns at the same moment, under the signing officer''s standing authorization. A car with a second owner on the ownership waits for that owner too: they get their own link by email and sign the same documents.

## Mark a car insured (Insurer confirmed)

A program owner''s car is handed over to a renter only once the insurer confirms in writing that it is on the fleet policy. Requests, offers and payment never wait for it.

1. Each car waiting for the insurer is a line on To do: "Insurer has not confirmed : mark it insured". It says Now when a booking picks the car up soon.
2. When the insurer''s email arrives, press **Mark insured**. The date is today; change it to the date of the insurer''s email if it was earlier. Add its subject as the Reference if you like, and press **Insurer confirmed**.
3. One email for several cars? Press **Mark several insured** on the line " cars wait for the insurer". Every waiting car is ticked: untick any car the insurer did not name, check the date, and confirm them all at once.
4. The same button is on the car: Overview (**Insurer confirmed**) and the Listing tab''s checklist, item "Not on the fleet insurance policy yet".

The car is then on the fleet policy from that date: it can be handed over, its Enrollment Date is that date, its fee terms start, and the owner gets the email "Written confirmation: your car is on the fleet policy". Its paperwork (agreements, registry visit, tracker) stays on its checklist until done. A car already listed and Available stays Available.

## Owners who paid another way, and the terms you agreed

Two lines on To do keep an owner''s money right without opening their page.

1. "Record the first and last month paid by ": their first and last month invoice was voided and nothing paid is recorded. Press **Record what they paid**, type the amount for each car (tax included), or one total for several cars, how and when it was paid and the reference. A draft first and last month invoice is kept or voided, your choice. Each car''s invoice is then marked paid and the two prepaid months count; the owner gets no email unless you tick **Email the owner a receipt**. Never for a shareholder.
2. "Enter the terms agreed with ": their cars still use the standard grid. Press **Enter the terms**: the Management fee (Revenue Share), the Insurance Fee, the Tracker Fee, the Install Fee and the first and last month are filled in from the grid. Type what you agreed for the owner, and open a car to give it its own. A car whose schedule is signed gets an updated schedule for the owner to sign.
3. Nothing to change? Press **Not needed** or **These are correct**: the line does not come back.

## A shareholder''s own car

On the owner''s page, each car has **Shareholder’s own car**.

1. A shareholder''s own car is split 90/10 (the share in Program settings) and pays no Insurance Fee, Tracker Fee, first and last month or tracker install.
2. Press **Shareholder’s own car**, say why (it is kept in the audit log) and confirm. Press it again to undo. Bookings already made keep their split.
3. A first and last month or a tracker install invoice is refused for such a car, from any screen.

## Cancellation refunds

**Settings** > **Program**: the refund for each cancellation tier.

| When the renter cancels | Refund (default) |
| --- | --- |
| Within 24 hours of booking, 48 hours or more before the start | 95% |
| 48 hours or more before the start | 75% |
| 24 to 48 hours before the start | 50% |
| Under 24 hours, or after the start | 0% |

## An owner''s page

Open an owner from Owners. Three tabs: Overview, Terms and Invoices. **Add another car** and **New invoice** sit under the name.

1. The **Onboarding checklist**, at the top: per car still onboarding, each step done, to do (with who it waits on: the owner, us, an Admin or the registry), blocked (with why) or not needed, and one button for the next thing to do. The owner and customer service see the same checklist.
2. Cars and terms: each car''s Insurance Fee, Tracker Fee, management fee (Revenue Share), Install Fee and mode, with **Edit** and History (see An owner''s terms, car by car).
3. **Onboarding photos**: the ownership permit, insurance slip and lender''s permission of each car. **Replace**, **Remove** (with a reason), **Approve** or **Not accepted** (the owner reads why). A replaced photo that was approved is checked again. Every change is in the audit log.
4. **Government forms**: the ServiceOntario forms each car needs, made by themselves when the terms are approved and again when a value changes, each with its status, what it misses, when it was made and its download. **Make again** makes a car''s forms anew now (a form signed in ink is kept); the values changed by hand stay, unless you tick **Discard the values changed by hand**. Open a form and press **Change a value** to correct one box of the official form before it is signed: choose the box, type the value and the reason. The form is made again as a new version; the earlier versions stay under **Versions**, each with its download, and every change is in the audit log. **Back to the records** puts a box''s value from the records again. The owner always sees the current version only. Fleet can do the same. The owner signs each form on screen during onboarding. Beside the form, **Owner''s signature** shows the drawn signature (or typed name), who signed, when, from which IP address and device, and the version signed; the signature is never on the official form, and **Download the print-ready form** has no signature. If you change a value after the owner signed, the form shows **Changed since signed** with the boxes that changed, the owner gets one To do (the government forms step opens again) and one reminder email, and the earlier signature stays under **Every signature**. The step is done when every form is signed.
5. **Add cars from a list of VINs**: paste or upload the VINs, **Preview**, then **Add**; a typo, a duplicate or a car already with us is reported, not added.
6. Upfront invoices: issue the first and last month amount agreed on each car''s terms, for each car whose terms are set.
7. Owner: address, sign-in and agreements; statements and payouts for this owner.
8. Further down: **View as (owner portal)**, **Send password link** and **Send a sign-in link to the owner portal**.

A car''s page has the same Government forms box (Owner & documents).

![](/guides/img/admin-13-owner-desktop-819a9f8b.jpg "desktop; size: 410 1030; address: carmacars.ca/admin/owners/50a834dc-270a-4c26-b79e-6396fa7bf2e1; pins: 1 24.6 4.4, 2 16.1 32.9, 3 31.5 73.2, 4 21.2 98.1")

## An owner''s terms, car by car

The table Cars and terms, at the top of an owner''s page and its Terms tab: each car''s Insurance Fee and Tracker Fee a month, management fee (Revenue Share), Install Fee and Management Mode, and since when they apply.

1. Press **Edit** on a car''s row. The row becomes fields: type the exact amounts (to the cent; the management fee in %). Before the Vehicle Schedule is signed you can also change the Install Fee, the Management Mode and the Onboarding Method.
2. Press **Review**. It lists each value before and after, and what happens to each one. Nothing is saved yet.
3. Not signed yet (or not approved yet): **Save** applies the numbers at once. An unsigned Vehicle Schedule is made again with them, so the owner signs these numbers; a car not approved yet keeps them for the Approve step.
4. Signed: a lower amount is in force from today, or the date you choose under Lower amounts from. No notice period is needed because it only lowers what the owner pays. A lower management fee does this while Settings > Program, Lower management % without owner signature, is on (the default); off, the owner signs an updated Vehicle Schedule first.
5. Signed: a higher Insurance Fee or Tracker Fee needs 30 days'' written notice (Enrollment Agreement 4.8). Choose the date under Higher amounts from (30 days ahead at the earliest) and write the Reason: the owner reads it.
6. Signed: a higher management fee (Revenue Share) needs the same notice and the owner''s signature. The owner is emailed the notice and an updated Vehicle Schedule to sign; it applies from the date once signed, or from the day they sign if that is later. Higher fees in the same change apply from the date by the notice either way.
7. Press **Confirm**. The owner is emailed the written notice, which is also a PDF in their portal and in the car''s History.

History, under each car, lists every period of terms (from, to, the amounts, and why: the Vehicle Schedule, a written notice, lowered) and every change with its notice. A change that has not started yet has Cancel (give the reason): the terms before it run on. An updated schedule waiting for the owner has Withdraw it; the owner signs it in the owner portal (never on paper). One change at a time: cancel or finish the one waiting before making the next.

The same editor is on the car''s page (Records tab, Owner terms). The owner''s default terms (for cars whose terms are set later) and the first and last month invoice stay on the Terms tab.

> Good to know: Invoices follow the dates: a month whose Insurance Fee or Tracker Fee changes part way is billed per day at each rate. The Revenue Share of a rental is the one in force on the day it is booked.

## Pay an owner a flat monthly amount

Some owners want the same amount every month for a car instead of a revenue share and fees. An Admin only, car by car.

1. Open the owner''s Cars and terms table (or the car''s page) and press **Pay** on the car''s row.
2. Choose **Flat monthly payment**, type the **Amount a month** (for example 900.00), the date under **From** and, if it ends, the **Last day**. Write the Reason (kept in the history).
3. Press **Review**: it says what happens and lists any monthly invoice already issued for those days. Then press **Confirm**.
4. From that date the owner''s statement pays the amount every month (a part month by the day), with no revenue share and no Insurance Fee or Tracker Fee. Rentals ending on those days stay with CarmaCars, in the company figures.
5. Back to revenue share: press **Pay**, choose Revenue share and the date. The flat period ends the day before; every period stays in the list.

> Good to know: A month already on an approved owner statement never changes: a new date starts after it. A monthly invoice already issued for flat days stays: void or credit it. A booking expense on a flat car is CarmaCars'' own unless you press **Charge to the owner** beside it on the booking (an Admin only): it is then an owner cost on their statement. Owner costs recorded on the owner''s account (tickets, tolls, damage of their own use) are charged as before.

## Change a signed car''s Management Mode

Managed, Self-Managed or Turo-Only, from a date, for a car whose Vehicle Schedule is signed. An Admin only.

1. Open the owner''s Cars and terms table (or the car''s page) and press **Change mode** on the car''s row.
2. Choose the **New Management Mode** and its Onboarding Method (the options that fit how the car is held), the date under **From**, and write the Reason: the owner reads it. Tick **The owner asked for this** only when it is their own request.
3. Press **Review**: it lists each value before and after (a Self-Managed car has no management fee; a Turo-Only car has no Fees and leaves the fleet insurance policy) and says whether the owner has to sign. Nothing is saved yet.
4. The owner asked and no amount goes up: no signature and no notice period. From today (or the date you chose) the car has the new mode, an updated Vehicle Schedule is issued with CarmaCars'' signature and the owner is emailed the notice.
5. Anything else (CarmaCars'' own decision, or a higher fee): the owner is emailed the notice and an updated Vehicle Schedule to sign, the date is at least 30 days away and the car stays as it is until it is signed. The owner signs it in the owner portal; in History, **Withdraw it** if needed.
6. A change dated ahead applies by itself on its date: the schedule is issued and the car moves. **Cancel** in History (give the reason) stops it and emails the owner that their terms stay as they are. The same email goes when a notice of a higher fee is cancelled.

> Good to know: A shareholder-owned car has fixed terms. A car whose schedule is not signed yet changes its mode in the terms editor, where it applies at once.

## Paid and signed

**People** > **Owners**, the **Paid and signed** tab. What each owner still has to pay or sign, and how each item was done.

1. Each owner shows how many items are open and how many are done. Owners with nothing left are hidden; press Show every owner to see them.
2. Open **Checklist and quick actions**. Each line says Signed in the portal, Signed on paper (before November 2026), Paid by e-Transfer, Not signed, and so on.
3. Paid by e-Transfer, cheque, cash or bank transfer? Press **Record payment**. Choose Paid by, the Date received and the Reference (the cheque number for a cheque). Leave Amount empty for the full balance, or type less for a partial payment. Add a photo of the cheque or a screenshot if you have one.
4. Every agreement is signed in the owner portal: a signature on paper is not recorded. Only an official ServiceOntario form signed in ink is: press **Record an official form signed in ink**, choose the form, check Signed by and Date signed, and upload the scan.
5. The same checklist sits at the top of each owner''s page.
6. You rarely need to come here: an upfront or overdue owner invoice is a line on To do with **Record payment**, and an owner whose documents were sent two days ago or more and are not signed is a line with **Waiting to sign** (open the owner to send the link again). Both pop-ups are the same forms, filled in.

A recorded payment marks the invoice paid (or partly paid), stops the automatic debit for that amount, sends the owner a receipt, and shows "Paid by e-Transfer on " in their portal. An official form recorded as signed in ink counts as signed everywhere: the checklist, onboarding and the owner portal. The scan is kept privately with the owner''s documents.

> Watch out: Recorded the wrong thing, or a cheque bounced? Press **Void** beside it and give the reason. The invoice owes that amount again and the owner is told; a voided signature makes the item open again. Only an Admin can void.

## Forms C and D

**People** > **Owner forms**. Forms C and D are signed on screen in the owner portal, with the witnesses on the same screen (one for Form C, two for Form D), and approved at once; Part 2 of Form D is signed for CarmaCars from the stored signatures (the signing officer, and the second signing officer of Program settings as CarmaCars'' witness). This queue holds only photos of paper copies sent before November 2026.

1. Each row shows the owner, the form, the witnesses and when it was uploaded.
2. Press Open to read the photo or scan. Check each marked spot is signed or initialled.
3. Press **Approve**, or **Send back** with What to fix (the owner reads this).

![](/guides/img/admin-22-owner-forms-desktop-c20ad300.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 470; address: carmacars.ca/admin/owner-forms; pins: 1 29.2 52.3, 2 57.6 52.3, 3 76.7 52.3")

## The earnings calculator on List your car

People who think of listing their car see what it could earn, near the top of List your car and, smaller, at the start of the application. Since release 48 the numbers are conservative and follow the season, and the result says plainly it is a rough estimate, not a promise.

They pick the year, make and model (or type the VIN), the **days rented in an average month** (4 to 22, 12 at first) and their share (60% to 90%, 70% at first, "set in your agreement"). The page then works a whole year, month by month:

- A month''s rented days are the days chosen times that month''s factor: summer runs above the average, winter under it, and the shoulder months (spring and fall) are the slowest.
- A rented day earns the daily rate of cars like theirs on the site (the same make and model, else the class average, else the class''s starting rate in Program settings) less a typical discount for weekly rates and offers.
- Their share of that, less the monthly fees.

It shows the average month, the year (the twelve months added up, never twelve of the best month), the range from the slowest month to the busiest, the rented days of each month as bars, and how many months the share would not cover the fees. "Just cheaper insurance" shows the fleet policy''s fee and what they would keep in their slowest month.

1. **Settings** > **Program**: **Earnings calculator on List your car: the monthly insurance fee shown** and **the monthly tracker fee shown**, in dollars a month.
2. Leave either one empty and the page says "Insurance and tracker fees: quoted in your agreement" and shows the earnings "before fees". No amount is ever made up.
3. Set both and the page takes them off every month and the year. Each owner''s real fees stay the ones in their agreement.
4. **Earnings calculator on List your car: the rented days of an average month it starts from** (12): keep it low, a new car takes months to fill.
5. **The percent that comes off the listed daily rate on a rented day** (15).
6. **The factor of each month** (jan to dec) against an average month (1.00): by default June 1.10, July and August 1.30, December 0.85, January and February 0.75, May and September 0.85, March and October 0.70, April and November 0.65. Every month must be there.

## Agreements: who still needs to sign

**Owners and partners** > **Owners** > **Agreements**. Every owner with the agreements their deal needs, and where each one stands.

1. Each owner shows their deal (revenue split, flat monthly or fleet lease) and one line per agreement: the Vehicle Enrollment Agreement, the Flat-Rate Vehicle Enrollment Agreement or the Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement, the Title-Holding and Lease Agreement, an Additional Vehicle Schedule for a car added later, the Partner agreement, and a Referral Override Agreement for each owner they referred.
2. Each line says **Signed**, **Sent, not signed**, **Not sent** or **Missing**. Missing means there is nothing to sign yet: set the terms of a car first, and the agreement is made from them.
3. Press **Send** (or **Send again**). The owner gets one email with the link to read and sign in their portal. An owner with no sign-in yet shows "invite first": press Invite on the Owners list.
4. Owners whose agreements are all signed are hidden; press Show every owner to see them. The same lines are at the top of each owner''s Terms tab.

> Good to know: "Awaiting lawyer OK" marks the Referral Override Agreement until the lawyer approves its text (Program settings). The Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement is approved. Owners can sign either way.

## A fleet supplier: the fleet lease

For a supplier''s corporation that leases many cars to CarmaCars. Open the owner, **Terms** tab, **Fleet lease**.

1. A supplier who signs up on the website as a fleet supplier (or whom staff add on the fleet supplier route) gets the default lease terms of Program settings and the default Upkeep Table at once: the card shows **Fleet supplier route**. To agree other numbers, press **Change the lease terms**.
2. A supplier on file without the route: press **Enter the lease terms** and type what you agreed: the Regular Rate and the Troubled Rate (the lease a month for each car of that tier), the Claim Profit Share, the Early Write-Off Share, the Write-Off Period in months, the Later Write-Off Share and the Notice Period in days.
3. Check the **Upkeep Table**: for each cost (engine, transmission, shocks, rustproofing, refurbishment, tires, brakes, oil changes, ball joints) the supplier or CarmaCars.
4. Add each car with **Add another car** on the owner''s page. The **Fleet lease** step asks for the tier (Regular or Troubled) and the delivery date: the tier is required and set once. No fee or invoice step: the supplier pays CarmaCars nothing, and no owner invoice or debit is ever made for these cars.
5. A car already on file: press **Put on the lease** beside it, with the delivery date and the tier.
6. The tier never changes. Typed the wrong one? Only an Admin can press **Correct the tier**, with what was entered by mistake. It is corrected from the delivery (or from the day after the last approved statement) and kept in the audit log.
7. The lease is paid in arrears on the 10th with the owner payouts: a car''s first payment is on the first 10th at least one full month after its delivery and covers every month up to then. Part months are paid by the day; the statement line shows the calculation (rate, days, total).
8. A claim on a leased car: settling it pays the supplier its Claim Profit Share of any profit, on its next statement. A write-off pays any lien first, then the supplier''s Early or Later Write-Off Share of the balance by the months in service.
9. An upkeep cost: **Record an upkeep cost**. A cost the Upkeep Table gives the supplier comes off its next lease payment; one CarmaCars pays is not billed.

> Watch out: New lease terms after the supplier signed wait for the supplier to sign the new agreement (it opens for signature at once). The cars keep the signed rates until then.

## Approve a fleet supplier''s cars

A supplier who signed up on the website: his application is in **Applications** like any other, with each car''s VIN, plate and the tier he chose.

1. Open the application. Check the ownership copy of each car (he uploads it in his portal), the tier and who the car is registered to now. Its ServiceOntario forms were filled in when he added it: the lease (SR-LV-006 with his corporation as the registrant, SR-LV-012 with CarmaCars holding the plates) and, for a car not yet in his corporation, the transfer (ON00453 when the corporation has no RIN; 013-0169 and 013-1155 when an officer moves his own car in). A form still missing a value (a RIN, the odometer) shows what is missing, as on the other routes.
2. A tier chosen by mistake: open the owner, **Terms** tab, **Fleet lease**, and press **Correct the tier** beside the car, with what was chosen by mistake. Only an Admin can, and only before approval; it is kept in the audit log.
3. Approve: there are no terms or invoices to set. Check **Delivered on** (the lease starts that day) and press **Approve**. Each car goes on the lease at its tier.
4. He signs in the owner portal only: the Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement and the Title-Holding and Lease Agreement, and Form B on screen, with the full e-signature and its audit trail. Paper signatures cannot be recorded for him. Form D is in his packet and signed on screen with two witnesses; Form C is not asked.

> Good to know: The Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement is final: the lawyer approved it, so it no longer shows "Awaiting lawyer OK". The default lease terms are in **Settings** > **Program settings** (Fleet supplier route); a change there applies to suppliers who sign up later.

> Good to know: Owners > **Add an owner** offers the same route: choose **A corporation**, then **Fleet supplier: leases the cars to CarmaCars**. So does **Add a car for an owner** for a new owner.

## Owner rewards (release 48)

1. **People** > **Owners** > **Owner rewards** shows the kits to ship, the upgrades to answer, each owner''s months and code, and what the rewards cost.
2. A merch kit to ship: when an owner presses Redeem on their Rewards tab, the kit shows here and on **To do** with the address they confirmed. Ship it, then press **Mark shipped** with the tracking number and what it cost. The owner is told and sees **Shipped**.
3. A free upgrade: when an owner''s car is down for a repair they say CarmaCars caused, they ask here. **Approve** with the amount CarmaCars covers (they get a one-time code), or **Decline** with the reason they read.
4. **Add a credit** gives an owner a credit by hand. Every credit is a line on the owner''s next statement and an expense in the books (Owner rewards and credits, account 5310).
5. What owners get: 20% off another car while theirs is out; a friends and family code (10% off a friend''s first rental, and the owner earns the 20% kickback); $100 for referring an owner once the new car has been live 30 days; a merch kit at 6 months and a premium kit at 12; a $25 birthday rental credit; priority support and early access.
6. Every number is in **Settings** > **Program settings** > **Owner rewards**.

## Sign first, then cars

Program setting: Sign first (on). An owner''s master agreement is made as soon as their profile is complete, with no car: the Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement with the Title-Holding and Lease Agreement for a fleet supplier, the Vehicle Enrollment Agreement otherwise. The owner signs it in the portal; CarmaCars countersigns at once with the signing officer of Settings.

- **Schedule A.** A supplier''s car gets its numbered Schedule A entry when it is added (one at a time, or Add cars from a list of VINs with a tier and plate per row) and its government forms then. A program owner''s car gets its entry when you set its terms. Cars added after the master is signed are confirmed by the owner with one signature per batch (the Additional Vehicle Schedule).
- **The gate.** A car is not approved (a supplier''s application), delivered (put on the lease) or rented (live) until the master agreement and its Schedule A entry are signed. Approving before the signature is kept: the application shows "Approved, waiting for the signature" and goes through by itself when the owner signs. If it cannot, you get a To do.
- **Agreements before cars.** The owner page and the application show exactly what is missing and who it waits on. Send reminder emails the owner (with the in-app notice and the push); once in 10 minutes at most.
- **Onboarding Method.** On the owner''s Terms tab, Change the method corrects a car''s method before its Vehicle Schedule is signed: the schedule, the plan and the government forms follow. The connector does the same with set_onboarding_method (previewed, then confirmed).
- **Document check** (Owners > Document check, and the connector''s owner_documents_check): anything still inconsistent on an owner''s documents, by owner, with what fixes it: a signing officer title that is a name (titles are roles, such as Director), a method that does not fit how the car is held (with none chosen, a car starts on Transfer, never Co-Registrant), a first and last month off the rule (two months of the Insurance Fee, which never carries HST), an empty value on a schedule.
- **Pickup not recorded.** A confirmed booking whose pickup was never recorded keeps its car presumed out after its return time: no new offer or booking goes on the car until you record the handover, the return or a no-show. Fleet gets the To do, then the Admins once the return time passed.
', 'Owners and onboarding', 'Applications, the terms and first invoice, adding a car for an owner, an owner''s terms and invoices, paid and signed, and Forms C and D.',
  'Owners apply on the site with List your car. Every application waits for you in one place, Applications: approve it, ask the owner for something, or decline it. Approved owners sign and pay in their portal.

## Applications

**People** > **Applications**. Every owner application, newest first.

1. The chips filter by status: New, Waiting on owner, Approved, Declined, or All. New applications also show on To do.
2. Each row shows the application number, the owner, the car, how many of the four checks are done, and when they applied.
3. Open an application to decide.

![](/guides/img/admin-33-applications-desktop-152f9e34.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 640; address: carmacars.ca/admin/applications; pins: 1 36.8 39.7, 2 48.6 53.1, 3 19.8 53.1")

## Decide on an application

One page holds everything: the owner, the car, the uploads, the four checks and the notes.

1. Check the driver''s licence, the ownership, the insurance and the lender or lessor. Mark each one Checked, fine, Problem or Not needed.
2. Press **Approve**. The step "Terms and first invoice" opens for each car, filled in with the owner''s negotiated terms (or the standard grid): Insurance Fee, Tracker Fee, management fee (Revenue Share), Install Fee and the first and last month amount (2 x the Insurance Fee unless you type an exact amount). Change any of them to the cent; with several cars, **Use these terms for every car** copies the first car''s numbers to the others.
3. Choose the invoices: First and last month, Registration fee (any exact amount), Tracker install (only once trackers are available) and Another invoice. For each one choose Send now, Save as draft or Already paid. Already paid asks how (e-Transfer, cash, cheque, bank transfer or other), the date and the reference: it is recorded like Record payment and the owner gets no email (no invoice, no receipt) unless you tick the receipt.
4. Press **Approve** at the bottom of the step. Nothing is set or sent before that. The owner becomes active, the documents open for one signature in their portal, only the invoices you chose are made, and the owner gets one email.
5. Missing something? Press **Ask for something**, tick what you need (for example the ownership permit or the insurance slip), add a message if you like, and press **Send to the owner**. The owner gets an email and a task in their portal; the application shows Waiting on owner until they answer.
6. Not a fit? Press **Decline**, write the Reason the owner reads, and press **Decline the application**. The owner is emailed for each car.

![](/guides/img/admin-34-application-desktop-98b64f92.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 812; address: carmacars.ca/admin/applications/c324ef8d-ad00-4bcc-bf04-ca68628a26b4; pins: 1 72.9 67.1, 2 73.9 42.9, 3 84.7 42.9, 4 72.9 49.6")

The application has an Invoices tab: every invoice of its cars, drafts and voids included. An application staff entered for the owner says "Entered by staff" and who; approving it sends the owner the set-up email (review the details and sign) instead of the approval email.

> Tip: Notes on the page are for staff only: **Add note** keeps a line on the record. When the owner answers a request, their answer is in the notes and the application is New again.

## Add a car for an owner

**People** > **Owners**, the **Add a car** tab, or **Add another car** on an owner''s page. The owner never has to fill in the application.

1. The owner: find them by name, email or phone, or choose New owner and enter the name, email, phone and address.
2. The car: press **Take a photo** (or **Choose a photo**) under Fill this from the ownership permit, and the plate, VIN, colour, permit number and plate sticker expiry fill in, with the year, make, model code and body read for you to check. Each detail shows Checked, Check this (for example a VIN that fails its check digit, a plate not in the usual format, or a sticker already expired) or Type it; the photo is attached as the ownership permit. Or type the VIN. The car is looked up at once and shown in one line (Edit if something is wrong); no VIN at hand, add it by its plate with the year, make and model from the lists. Tap the colour, check the class, then the odometer, insurer and whether it is owned, financed or leased. Photos are optional: the listing shows sample photos until real ones are added. Upload the ownership permit, the insurance slip and the lender''s information if you have them.
3. Terms and first invoice: the same fields as Approve. For another car of the same owner they start from that owner''s terms, or their other car''s; change them for this car.
4. Who sourced the owner: Entered for CarmaCars, or I sourced this owner (only then are you recorded as the one who brought the owner). The owner signs in the owner portal after one email (no paper signature).
5. Press **Add the car and set it up**. The owner gets one email: review the details, correct anything, and sign. An owner with no sign-in gets the link to choose a password in that same email.

Customer service and fleet assistants add cars the same way from their portal; theirs wait in Applications for you, with the terms and invoices they proposed already filled in. On an approved application staff entered, **Send the set-up email again** sends the owner the email with a fresh link.

## Owners

**People** > **Owners**. Every owner, with their cars and where onboarding stands.

1. Each owner shows their application, how many cars, and where onboarding stands.
2. **View as (owner portal)** shows their portal. **Send password link** helps them sign in.
3. Invite an owner on file: fill in Name and Email under Invite an owner, then press **Send invitation**.

![](/guides/img/admin-12-owners-desktop-3a54d505.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 560; address: carmacars.ca/admin/owners; pins: 1 41.0 42.9, 2 37.4 49.3, 3 77.4 82.5")

The owner signs everything at once in their portal (Check and sign: the agreements, schedules and Forms A and B; the official registry forms are printed and signed in ink). The confirmations to tick, then one signature: CarmaCars countersigns at the same moment, under the signing officer''s standing authorization. A car with a second owner on the ownership waits for that owner too: they get their own link by email and sign the same documents.

## Mark a car insured (Insurer confirmed)

A program owner''s car is handed over to a renter only once the insurer confirms in writing that it is on the fleet policy. Requests, offers and payment never wait for it.

1. Each car waiting for the insurer is a line on To do: "Insurer has not confirmed : mark it insured". It says Now when a booking picks the car up soon.
2. When the insurer''s email arrives, press **Mark insured**. The date is today; change it to the date of the insurer''s email if it was earlier. Add its subject as the Reference if you like, and press **Insurer confirmed**.
3. One email for several cars? Press **Mark several insured** on the line " cars wait for the insurer". Every waiting car is ticked: untick any car the insurer did not name, check the date, and confirm them all at once.
4. The same button is on the car: Overview (**Insurer confirmed**) and the Listing tab''s checklist, item "Not on the fleet insurance policy yet".

The car is then on the fleet policy from that date: it can be handed over, its Enrollment Date is that date, its fee terms start, and the owner gets the email "Written confirmation: your car is on the fleet policy". Its paperwork (agreements, registry visit, tracker) stays on its checklist until done. A car already listed and Available stays Available.

## Owners who paid another way, and the terms you agreed

Two lines on To do keep an owner''s money right without opening their page.

1. "Record the first and last month paid by ": their first and last month invoice was voided and nothing paid is recorded. Press **Record what they paid**, type the amount for each car (tax included), or one total for several cars, how and when it was paid and the reference. A draft first and last month invoice is kept or voided, your choice. Each car''s invoice is then marked paid and the two prepaid months count; the owner gets no email unless you tick **Email the owner a receipt**. Never for a shareholder.
2. "Enter the terms agreed with ": their cars still use the standard grid. Press **Enter the terms**: the Management fee (Revenue Share), the Insurance Fee, the Tracker Fee, the Install Fee and the first and last month are filled in from the grid. Type what you agreed for the owner, and open a car to give it its own. A car whose schedule is signed gets an updated schedule for the owner to sign.
3. Nothing to change? Press **Not needed** or **These are correct**: the line does not come back.

## A shareholder''s own car

On the owner''s page, each car has **Shareholder’s own car**.

1. A shareholder''s own car is split 90/10 (the share in Program settings) and pays no Insurance Fee, Tracker Fee, first and last month or tracker install.
2. Press **Shareholder’s own car**, say why (it is kept in the audit log) and confirm. Press it again to undo. Bookings already made keep their split.
3. A first and last month or a tracker install invoice is refused for such a car, from any screen.

## Cancellation refunds

**Settings** > **Program**: the refund for each cancellation tier.

| When the renter cancels | Refund (default) |
| --- | --- |
| Within 24 hours of booking, 48 hours or more before the start | 95% |
| 48 hours or more before the start | 75% |
| 24 to 48 hours before the start | 50% |
| Under 24 hours, or after the start | 0% |

## An owner''s page

Open an owner from Owners. Three tabs: Overview, Terms and Invoices. **Add another car** and **New invoice** sit under the name.

1. The **Onboarding checklist**, at the top: per car still onboarding, each step done, to do (with who it waits on: the owner, us, an Admin or the registry), blocked (with why) or not needed, and one button for the next thing to do. The owner and customer service see the same checklist.
2. Cars and terms: each car''s Insurance Fee, Tracker Fee, management fee (Revenue Share), Install Fee and mode, with **Edit** and History (see An owner''s terms, car by car).
3. **Onboarding photos**: the ownership permit, insurance slip and lender''s permission of each car. **Replace**, **Remove** (with a reason), **Approve** or **Not accepted** (the owner reads why). A replaced photo that was approved is checked again. Every change is in the audit log.
4. **Government forms**: the ServiceOntario forms each car needs, made by themselves when the terms are approved and again when a value changes, each with its status, what it misses, when it was made and its download. **Make again** makes a car''s forms anew now (a form signed in ink is kept); the values changed by hand stay, unless you tick **Discard the values changed by hand**. Open a form and press **Change a value** to correct one box of the official form before it is signed: choose the box, type the value and the reason. The form is made again as a new version; the earlier versions stay under **Versions**, each with its download, and every change is in the audit log. **Back to the records** puts a box''s value from the records again. The owner always sees the current version only. Fleet can do the same. The owner signs each form on screen during onboarding. Beside the form, **Owner''s signature** shows the drawn signature (or typed name), who signed, when, from which IP address and device, and the version signed; the signature is never on the official form, and **Download the print-ready form** has no signature. If you change a value after the owner signed, the form shows **Changed since signed** with the boxes that changed, the owner gets one To do (the government forms step opens again) and one reminder email, and the earlier signature stays under **Every signature**. The step is done when every form is signed.
5. **Add cars from a list of VINs**: paste or upload the VINs, **Preview**, then **Add**; a typo, a duplicate or a car already with us is reported, not added.
6. Upfront invoices: issue the first and last month amount agreed on each car''s terms, for each car whose terms are set.
7. Owner: address, sign-in and agreements; statements and payouts for this owner.
8. Further down: **View as (owner portal)**, **Send password link** and **Send a sign-in link to the owner portal**.

A car''s page has the same Government forms box (Owner & documents).

![](/guides/img/admin-13-owner-desktop-819a9f8b.jpg "desktop; size: 410 1030; address: carmacars.ca/admin/owners/50a834dc-270a-4c26-b79e-6396fa7bf2e1; pins: 1 24.6 4.4, 2 16.1 32.9, 3 31.5 73.2, 4 21.2 98.1")

## An owner''s terms, car by car

The table Cars and terms, at the top of an owner''s page and its Terms tab: each car''s Insurance Fee and Tracker Fee a month, management fee (Revenue Share), Install Fee and Management Mode, and since when they apply.

1. Press **Edit** on a car''s row. The row becomes fields: type the exact amounts (to the cent; the management fee in %). Before the Vehicle Schedule is signed you can also change the Install Fee, the Management Mode and the Onboarding Method.
2. Press **Review**. It lists each value before and after, and what happens to each one. Nothing is saved yet.
3. Not signed yet (or not approved yet): **Save** applies the numbers at once. An unsigned Vehicle Schedule is made again with them, so the owner signs these numbers; a car not approved yet keeps them for the Approve step.
4. Signed: a lower amount is in force from today, or the date you choose under Lower amounts from. No notice period is needed because it only lowers what the owner pays. A lower management fee does this while Settings > Program, Lower management % without owner signature, is on (the default); off, the owner signs an updated Vehicle Schedule first.
5. Signed: a higher Insurance Fee or Tracker Fee needs 30 days'' written notice (Enrollment Agreement 4.8). Choose the date under Higher amounts from (30 days ahead at the earliest) and write the Reason: the owner reads it.
6. Signed: a higher management fee (Revenue Share) needs the same notice and the owner''s signature. The owner is emailed the notice and an updated Vehicle Schedule to sign; it applies from the date once signed, or from the day they sign if that is later. Higher fees in the same change apply from the date by the notice either way.
7. Press **Confirm**. The owner is emailed the written notice, which is also a PDF in their portal and in the car''s History.

History, under each car, lists every period of terms (from, to, the amounts, and why: the Vehicle Schedule, a written notice, lowered) and every change with its notice. A change that has not started yet has Cancel (give the reason): the terms before it run on. An updated schedule waiting for the owner has Withdraw it; the owner signs it in the owner portal (never on paper). One change at a time: cancel or finish the one waiting before making the next.

The same editor is on the car''s page (Records tab, Owner terms). The owner''s default terms (for cars whose terms are set later) and the first and last month invoice stay on the Terms tab.

> Good to know: Invoices follow the dates: a month whose Insurance Fee or Tracker Fee changes part way is billed per day at each rate. The Revenue Share of a rental is the one in force on the day it is booked.

## Pay an owner a flat monthly amount

Some owners want the same amount every month for a car instead of a revenue share and fees. An Admin only, car by car.

1. Open the owner''s Cars and terms table (or the car''s page) and press **Pay** on the car''s row.
2. Choose **Flat monthly payment**, type the **Amount a month** (for example 900.00), the date under **From** and, if it ends, the **Last day**. Write the Reason (kept in the history).
3. Press **Review**: it says what happens and lists any monthly invoice already issued for those days. Then press **Confirm**.
4. From that date the owner''s statement pays the amount every month (a part month by the day), with no revenue share and no Insurance Fee or Tracker Fee. Rentals ending on those days stay with CarmaCars, in the company figures.
5. Back to revenue share: press **Pay**, choose Revenue share and the date. The flat period ends the day before; every period stays in the list.

> Good to know: A month already on an approved owner statement never changes: a new date starts after it. A monthly invoice already issued for flat days stays: void or credit it. A booking expense on a flat car is CarmaCars'' own unless you press **Charge to the owner** beside it on the booking (an Admin only): it is then an owner cost on their statement. Owner costs recorded on the owner''s account (tickets, tolls, damage of their own use) are charged as before.

## Change a signed car''s Management Mode

Managed, Self-Managed or Turo-Only, from a date, for a car whose Vehicle Schedule is signed. An Admin only.

1. Open the owner''s Cars and terms table (or the car''s page) and press **Change mode** on the car''s row.
2. Choose the **New Management Mode** and its Onboarding Method (the options that fit how the car is held), the date under **From**, and write the Reason: the owner reads it. Tick **The owner asked for this** only when it is their own request.
3. Press **Review**: it lists each value before and after (a Self-Managed car has no management fee; a Turo-Only car has no Fees and leaves the fleet insurance policy) and says whether the owner has to sign. Nothing is saved yet.
4. The owner asked and no amount goes up: no signature and no notice period. From today (or the date you chose) the car has the new mode, an updated Vehicle Schedule is issued with CarmaCars'' signature and the owner is emailed the notice.
5. Anything else (CarmaCars'' own decision, or a higher fee): the owner is emailed the notice and an updated Vehicle Schedule to sign, the date is at least 30 days away and the car stays as it is until it is signed. The owner signs it in the owner portal; in History, **Withdraw it** if needed.
6. A change dated ahead applies by itself on its date: the schedule is issued and the car moves. **Cancel** in History (give the reason) stops it and emails the owner that their terms stay as they are. The same email goes when a notice of a higher fee is cancelled.

> Good to know: A shareholder-owned car has fixed terms. A car whose schedule is not signed yet changes its mode in the terms editor, where it applies at once.

## Paid and signed

**People** > **Owners**, the **Paid and signed** tab. What each owner still has to pay or sign, and how each item was done.

1. Each owner shows how many items are open and how many are done. Owners with nothing left are hidden; press Show every owner to see them.
2. Open **Checklist and quick actions**. Each line says Signed in the portal, Signed on paper (before November 2026), Paid by e-Transfer, Not signed, and so on.
3. Paid by e-Transfer, cheque, cash or bank transfer? Press **Record payment**. Choose Paid by, the Date received and the Reference (the cheque number for a cheque). Leave Amount empty for the full balance, or type less for a partial payment. Add a photo of the cheque or a screenshot if you have one.
4. Every agreement is signed in the owner portal: a signature on paper is not recorded. Only an official ServiceOntario form signed in ink is: press **Record an official form signed in ink**, choose the form, check Signed by and Date signed, and upload the scan.
5. The same checklist sits at the top of each owner''s page.
6. You rarely need to come here: an upfront or overdue owner invoice is a line on To do with **Record payment**, and an owner whose documents were sent two days ago or more and are not signed is a line with **Waiting to sign** (open the owner to send the link again). Both pop-ups are the same forms, filled in.

A recorded payment marks the invoice paid (or partly paid), stops the automatic debit for that amount, sends the owner a receipt, and shows "Paid by e-Transfer on " in their portal. An official form recorded as signed in ink counts as signed everywhere: the checklist, onboarding and the owner portal. The scan is kept privately with the owner''s documents.

> Watch out: Recorded the wrong thing, or a cheque bounced? Press **Void** beside it and give the reason. The invoice owes that amount again and the owner is told; a voided signature makes the item open again. Only an Admin can void.

## Forms C and D

**People** > **Owner forms**. Forms C and D are signed on screen in the owner portal, with the witnesses on the same screen (one for Form C, two for Form D), and approved at once; Part 2 of Form D is signed for CarmaCars from the stored signatures (the signing officer, and the second signing officer of Program settings as CarmaCars'' witness). This queue holds only photos of paper copies sent before November 2026.

1. Each row shows the owner, the form, the witnesses and when it was uploaded.
2. Press Open to read the photo or scan. Check each marked spot is signed or initialled.
3. Press **Approve**, or **Send back** with What to fix (the owner reads this).

![](/guides/img/admin-22-owner-forms-desktop-c20ad300.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 470; address: carmacars.ca/admin/owner-forms; pins: 1 29.2 52.3, 2 57.6 52.3, 3 76.7 52.3")

## The earnings calculator on List your car

People who think of listing their car see what it could earn, near the top of List your car and, smaller, at the start of the application. Since release 48 the numbers are conservative and follow the season, and the result says plainly it is a rough estimate, not a promise.

They pick the year, make and model (or type the VIN), the **days rented in an average month** (4 to 22, 12 at first) and their share (60% to 90%, 70% at first, "set in your agreement"). The page then works a whole year, month by month:

- A month''s rented days are the days chosen times that month''s factor: summer runs above the average, winter under it, and the shoulder months (spring and fall) are the slowest.
- A rented day earns the daily rate of cars like theirs on the site (the same make and model, else the class average, else the class''s starting rate in Program settings) less a typical discount for weekly rates and offers.
- Their share of that, less the monthly fees.

It shows the average month, the year (the twelve months added up, never twelve of the best month), the range from the slowest month to the busiest, the rented days of each month as bars, and how many months the share would not cover the fees. "Just cheaper insurance" shows the fleet policy''s fee and what they would keep in their slowest month.

1. **Settings** > **Program**: **Earnings calculator on List your car: the monthly insurance fee shown** and **the monthly tracker fee shown**, in dollars a month.
2. Leave either one empty and the page says "Insurance and tracker fees: quoted in your agreement" and shows the earnings "before fees". No amount is ever made up.
3. Set both and the page takes them off every month and the year. Each owner''s real fees stay the ones in their agreement.
4. **Earnings calculator on List your car: the rented days of an average month it starts from** (12): keep it low, a new car takes months to fill.
5. **The percent that comes off the listed daily rate on a rented day** (15).
6. **The factor of each month** (jan to dec) against an average month (1.00): by default June 1.10, July and August 1.30, December 0.85, January and February 0.75, May and September 0.85, March and October 0.70, April and November 0.65. Every month must be there.

## Agreements: who still needs to sign

**Owners and partners** > **Owners** > **Agreements**. Every owner with the agreements their deal needs, and where each one stands.

1. Each owner shows their deal (revenue split, flat monthly or fleet lease) and one line per agreement: the Vehicle Enrollment Agreement, the Flat-Rate Vehicle Enrollment Agreement or the Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement, the Title-Holding and Lease Agreement, an Additional Vehicle Schedule for a car added later, the Partner agreement, and a Referral Override Agreement for each owner they referred.
2. Each line says **Signed**, **Sent, not signed**, **Not sent** or **Missing**. Missing means there is nothing to sign yet: set the terms of a car first, and the agreement is made from them.
3. Press **Send** (or **Send again**). The owner gets one email with the link to read and sign in their portal. An owner with no sign-in yet shows "invite first": press Invite on the Owners list.
4. Owners whose agreements are all signed are hidden; press Show every owner to see them. The same lines are at the top of each owner''s Terms tab.

> Good to know: "Awaiting lawyer OK" marks the Referral Override Agreement until the lawyer approves its text (Program settings). The Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement is approved. Owners can sign either way.

## A fleet supplier: the fleet lease

For a supplier''s corporation that leases many cars to CarmaCars. Open the owner, **Terms** tab, **Fleet lease**.

1. A supplier who signs up on the website as a fleet supplier (or whom staff add on the fleet supplier route) gets the default lease terms of Program settings and the default Upkeep Table at once: the card shows **Fleet supplier route**. To agree other numbers, press **Change the lease terms**.
2. A supplier on file without the route: press **Enter the lease terms** and type what you agreed: the Regular Rate and the Troubled Rate (the lease a month for each car of that tier), the Claim Profit Share, the Early Write-Off Share, the Write-Off Period in months, the Later Write-Off Share and the Notice Period in days.
3. Check the **Upkeep Table**: for each cost (engine, transmission, shocks, rustproofing, refurbishment, tires, brakes, oil changes, ball joints) the supplier or CarmaCars.
4. Add each car with **Add another car** on the owner''s page. The **Fleet lease** step asks for the tier (Regular or Troubled) and the delivery date: the tier is required and set once. No fee or invoice step: the supplier pays CarmaCars nothing, and no owner invoice or debit is ever made for these cars.
5. A car already on file: press **Put on the lease** beside it, with the delivery date and the tier.
6. The tier never changes. Typed the wrong one? Only an Admin can press **Correct the tier**, with what was entered by mistake. It is corrected from the delivery (or from the day after the last approved statement) and kept in the audit log.
7. The lease is paid in arrears on the 10th with the owner payouts: a car''s first payment is on the first 10th at least one full month after its delivery and covers every month up to then. Part months are paid by the day; the statement line shows the calculation (rate, days, total).
8. A claim on a leased car: settling it pays the supplier its Claim Profit Share of any profit, on its next statement. A write-off pays any lien first, then the supplier''s Early or Later Write-Off Share of the balance by the months in service.
9. An upkeep cost: **Record an upkeep cost**. A cost the Upkeep Table gives the supplier comes off its next lease payment; one CarmaCars pays is not billed.

> Watch out: New lease terms after the supplier signed wait for the supplier to sign the new agreement (it opens for signature at once). The cars keep the signed rates until then.

## Approve a fleet supplier''s cars

A supplier who signed up on the website: his application is in **Applications** like any other, with each car''s VIN, plate and the tier he chose.

1. Open the application. Check the ownership copy of each car (he uploads it in his portal), the tier and who the car is registered to now. Its ServiceOntario forms were filled in when he added it: the lease (SR-LV-006 with his corporation as the registrant, SR-LV-012 with CarmaCars holding the plates) and, for a car not yet in his corporation, the transfer (ON00453 when the corporation has no RIN; 013-0169 and 013-1155 when an officer moves his own car in). A form still missing a value (a RIN, the odometer) shows what is missing, as on the other routes.
2. A tier chosen by mistake: open the owner, **Terms** tab, **Fleet lease**, and press **Correct the tier** beside the car, with what was chosen by mistake. Only an Admin can, and only before approval; it is kept in the audit log.
3. Approve: there are no terms or invoices to set. Check **Delivered on** (the lease starts that day) and press **Approve**. Each car goes on the lease at its tier.
4. He signs in the owner portal only: the Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement and the Title-Holding and Lease Agreement, and Form B on screen, with the full e-signature and its audit trail. Paper signatures cannot be recorded for him. Form D is in his packet and signed on screen with two witnesses; Form C is not asked.

> Good to know: The Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement is final: the lawyer approved it, so it no longer shows "Awaiting lawyer OK". The default lease terms are in **Settings** > **Program settings** (Fleet supplier route); a change there applies to suppliers who sign up later.

> Good to know: Owners > **Add an owner** offers the same route: choose **A corporation**, then **Fleet supplier: leases the cars to CarmaCars**. So does **Add a car for an owner** for a new owner.

## Owner rewards (release 48)

1. **People** > **Owners** > **Owner rewards** shows the kits to ship, the upgrades to answer, each owner''s months and code, and what the rewards cost.
2. A merch kit to ship: when an owner presses Redeem on their Rewards tab, the kit shows here and on **To do** with the address they confirmed. Ship it, then press **Mark shipped** with the tracking number and what it cost. The owner is told and sees **Shipped**.
3. A free upgrade: when an owner''s car is down for a repair they say CarmaCars caused, they ask here. **Approve** with the amount CarmaCars covers (they get a one-time code), or **Decline** with the reason they read.
4. **Add a credit** gives an owner a credit by hand. Every credit is a line on the owner''s next statement and an expense in the books (Owner rewards and credits, account 5310).
5. What owners get: 20% off another car while theirs is out; a friends and family code (10% off a friend''s first rental, and the owner earns the 20% kickback); $100 for referring an owner once the new car has been live 30 days; a merch kit at 6 months and a premium kit at 12; a $25 birthday rental credit; priority support and early access.
6. Every number is in **Settings** > **Program settings** > **Owner rewards**.

## Sign first, then cars

Program setting: Sign first (on). An owner''s master agreement is made as soon as their profile is complete, with no car: the Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement with the Title-Holding and Lease Agreement for a fleet supplier, the Vehicle Enrollment Agreement otherwise. The owner signs it in the portal; CarmaCars countersigns at once with the signing officer of Settings.

- **Schedule A.** A supplier''s car gets its numbered Schedule A entry when it is added (one at a time, or Add cars from a list of VINs with a tier and plate per row) and its government forms then. A program owner''s car gets its entry when you set its terms. Cars added after the master is signed are confirmed by the owner with one signature per batch (the Additional Vehicle Schedule).
- **The gate.** A car is not approved (a supplier''s application), delivered (put on the lease) or rented (live) until the master agreement and its Schedule A entry are signed. Approving before the signature is kept: the application shows "Approved, waiting for the signature" and goes through by itself when the owner signs. If it cannot, you get a To do.
- **Agreements before cars.** The owner page and the application show exactly what is missing and who it waits on. Send reminder emails the owner (with the in-app notice and the push); once in 10 minutes at most.
- **Onboarding Method.** On the owner''s Terms tab, Change the method corrects a car''s method before its Vehicle Schedule is signed: the schedule, the plan and the government forms follow. The connector does the same with set_onboarding_method (previewed, then confirmed).
- **Document check** (Owners > Document check, and the connector''s owner_documents_check): anything still inconsistent on an owner''s documents, by owner, with what fixes it: a signing officer title that is a name (titles are roles, such as Director), a method that does not fit how the car is held (with none chosen, a car starts on Transfer, never Co-Registrant), a first and last month off the rule (two months of the Insurance Fee, which never carries HST), an empty value on a schedule.
- **Pickup not recorded.** A confirmed booking whose pickup was never recorded keeps its car presumed out after its return time: no new offer or booking goes on the car until you record the handover, the return or a no-show. Fleet gets the To do, then the Admins once the return time passed.
- Onboarding steps, the owner pipeline: At the top of the owner page: each car''s route (Transfer, Co-Registrant, Lease, Lease through a new Owner Corporation), every step done or not, and the current one with whose turn it is, its one action, what to bring, where to go, the expected time and the blockers. **Advance this step** marks the current step done; **Override a step** sets any step done, not needed, open again or back to the records. Both need a reason and are kept in the audit log. You get a To do when a step is yours (terms, listing); a step waiting 3 days (Program settings, owner_stage_stall_days) emails you. **Marketing > Owner pipeline** shows every car by step, with the nudge and the call script.
- **Incorporation referral** (Settings): owners who lease through a new corporation get Incorporate now with the provider''s affiliate link. Off until you paste the link; each owner who opens it is listed with their code; mark Incorporated and Commission received from the provider''s report.
',
  '<p class="gd-p">Owners apply on the site with List your car. Every application waits for you in one place, Applications: approve it, ask the owner for something, or decline it. Approved owners sign and pay in their portal.</p><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-applications" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Applications</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Applications</b>. Every owner application, newest first.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The chips filter by status: New, Waiting on owner, Approved, Declined, or All. New applications also show on To do.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Each row shows the application number, the owner, the car, how many of the four checks are done, and when they applied.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Open an application to decide.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/applications</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/640"><img src="/guides/img/admin-33-applications-desktop-152f9e34.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="640"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:36.8%;top:39.7%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:48.6%;top:53.1%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:19.8%;top:53.1%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-decide-on-an-application" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Decide on an application</h2><p class="gd-p">One page holds everything: the owner, the car, the uploads, the four checks and the notes.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Check the driver&#39;s licence, the ownership, the insurance and the lender or lessor. Mark each one Checked, fine, Problem or Not needed.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b>. The step &quot;Terms and first invoice&quot; opens for each car, filled in with the owner&#39;s negotiated terms (or the standard grid): Insurance Fee, Tracker Fee, management fee (Revenue Share), Install Fee and the first and last month amount (2 x the Insurance Fee unless you type an exact amount). Change any of them to the cent; with several cars, <b class="gd-ui">Use these terms for every car</b> copies the first car&#39;s numbers to the others.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the invoices: First and last month, Registration fee (any exact amount), Tracker install (only once trackers are available) and Another invoice. For each one choose Send now, Save as draft or Already paid. Already paid asks how (e-Transfer, cash, cheque, bank transfer or other), the date and the reference: it is recorded like Record payment and the owner gets no email (no invoice, no receipt) unless you tick the receipt.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b> at the bottom of the step. Nothing is set or sent before that. The owner becomes active, the documents open for one signature in their portal, only the invoices you chose are made, and the owner gets one email.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Missing something? Press <b class="gd-ui">Ask for something</b>, tick what you need (for example the ownership permit or the insurance slip), add a message if you like, and press <b class="gd-ui">Send to the owner</b>. The owner gets an email and a task in their portal; the application shows Waiting on owner until they answer.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Not a fit? Press <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b>, write the Reason the owner reads, and press <b class="gd-ui">Decline the application</b>. The owner is emailed for each car.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/applications/c324ef8d-ad00-4bcc-bf04-ca68628a26b4</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/812"><img src="/guides/img/admin-34-application-desktop-98b64f92.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="812"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:72.9%;top:67.1%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:73.9%;top:42.9%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:84.7%;top:42.9%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:72.9%;top:49.6%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div><p class="gd-p">The application has an Invoices tab: every invoice of its cars, drafts and voids included. An application staff entered for the owner says &quot;Entered by staff&quot; and who; approving it sends the owner the set-up email (review the details and sign) instead of the approval email.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Notes on the page are for staff only: <b class="gd-ui">Add note</b> keeps a line on the record. When the owner answers a request, their answer is in the notes and the application is New again.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-add-a-car-for-an-owner" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Add a car for an owner</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owners</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Add a car</b> tab, or <b class="gd-ui">Add another car</b> on an owner&#39;s page. The owner never has to fill in the application.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The owner: find them by name, email or phone, or choose New owner and enter the name, email, phone and address.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The car: press <b class="gd-ui">Take a photo</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Choose a photo</b>) under Fill this from the ownership permit, and the plate, VIN, colour, permit number and plate sticker expiry fill in, with the year, make, model code and body read for you to check. Each detail shows Checked, Check this (for example a VIN that fails its check digit, a plate not in the usual format, or a sticker already expired) or Type it; the photo is attached as the ownership permit. Or type the VIN. The car is looked up at once and shown in one line (Edit if something is wrong); no VIN at hand, add it by its plate with the year, make and model from the lists. Tap the colour, check the class, then the odometer, insurer and whether it is owned, financed or leased. Photos are optional: the listing shows sample photos until real ones are added. Upload the ownership permit, the insurance slip and the lender&#39;s information if you have them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Terms and first invoice: the same fields as Approve. For another car of the same owner they start from that owner&#39;s terms, or their other car&#39;s; change them for this car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Who sourced the owner: Entered for CarmaCars, or I sourced this owner (only then are you recorded as the one who brought the owner). The owner signs in the owner portal after one email (no paper signature).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Add the car and set it up</b>. The owner gets one email: review the details, correct anything, and sign. An owner with no sign-in gets the link to choose a password in that same email.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Customer service and fleet assistants add cars the same way from their portal; theirs wait in Applications for you, with the terms and invoices they proposed already filled in. On an approved application staff entered, <b class="gd-ui">Send the set-up email again</b> sends the owner the email with a fresh link.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-owners" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Owners</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owners</b>. Every owner, with their cars and where onboarding stands.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each owner shows their application, how many cars, and where onboarding stands.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">View as (owner portal)</b> shows their portal. <b class="gd-ui">Send password link</b> helps them sign in.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Invite an owner on file: fill in Name and Email under Invite an owner, then press <b class="gd-ui">Send invitation</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/owners</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/560"><img src="/guides/img/admin-12-owners-desktop-3a54d505.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="560"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:41%;top:42.9%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:37.4%;top:49.3%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:77.4%;top:82.5%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div><p class="gd-p">The owner signs everything at once in their portal (Check and sign: the agreements, schedules and Forms A and B; the official registry forms are printed and signed in ink). The confirmations to tick, then one signature: CarmaCars countersigns at the same moment, under the signing officer&#39;s standing authorization. A car with a second owner on the ownership waits for that owner too: they get their own link by email and sign the same documents.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-mark-a-car-insured-insurer-confirmed" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Mark a car insured (Insurer confirmed)</h2><p class="gd-p">A program owner&#39;s car is handed over to a renter only once the insurer confirms in writing that it is on the fleet policy. Requests, offers and payment never wait for it.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each car waiting for the insurer is a line on To do: &quot;Insurer has not confirmed : mark it insured&quot;. It says Now when a booking picks the car up soon.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">When the insurer&#39;s email arrives, press <b class="gd-ui">Mark insured</b>. The date is today; change it to the date of the insurer&#39;s email if it was earlier. Add its subject as the Reference if you like, and press <b class="gd-ui">Insurer confirmed</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">One email for several cars? Press <b class="gd-ui">Mark several insured</b> on the line &quot; cars wait for the insurer&quot;. Every waiting car is ticked: untick any car the insurer did not name, check the date, and confirm them all at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The same button is on the car: Overview (<b class="gd-ui">Insurer confirmed</b>) and the Listing tab&#39;s checklist, item &quot;Not on the fleet insurance policy yet&quot;.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">The car is then on the fleet policy from that date: it can be handed over, its Enrollment Date is that date, its fee terms start, and the owner gets the email &quot;Written confirmation: your car is on the fleet policy&quot;. Its paperwork (agreements, registry visit, tracker) stays on its checklist until done. A car already listed and Available stays Available.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-owners-who-paid-another-way-and-the-terms-you-agreed" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Owners who paid another way, and the terms you agreed</h2><p class="gd-p">Two lines on To do keep an owner&#39;s money right without opening their page.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">&quot;Record the first and last month paid by &quot;: their first and last month invoice was voided and nothing paid is recorded. Press <b class="gd-ui">Record what they paid</b>, type the amount for each car (tax included), or one total for several cars, how and when it was paid and the reference. A draft first and last month invoice is kept or voided, your choice. Each car&#39;s invoice is then marked paid and the two prepaid months count; the owner gets no email unless you tick <b class="gd-ui">Email the owner a receipt</b>. Never for a shareholder.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">&quot;Enter the terms agreed with &quot;: their cars still use the standard grid. Press <b class="gd-ui">Enter the terms</b>: the Management fee (Revenue Share), the Insurance Fee, the Tracker Fee, the Install Fee and the first and last month are filled in from the grid. Type what you agreed for the owner, and open a car to give it its own. A car whose schedule is signed gets an updated schedule for the owner to sign.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Nothing to change? Press <b class="gd-ui">Not needed</b> or <b class="gd-ui">These are correct</b>: the line does not come back.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-a-shareholder-s-own-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A shareholder&#39;s own car</h2><p class="gd-p">On the owner&#39;s page, each car has <b class="gd-ui">Shareholder’s own car</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A shareholder&#39;s own car is split 90/10 (the share in Program settings) and pays no Insurance Fee, Tracker Fee, first and last month or tracker install.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Shareholder’s own car</b>, say why (it is kept in the audit log) and confirm. Press it again to undo. Bookings already made keep their split.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A first and last month or a tracker install invoice is refused for such a car, from any screen.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-cancellation-refunds" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Cancellation refunds</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>: the refund for each cancellation tier.</p><div class="gd-tablewrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Table"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">When the renter cancels</th><th scope="col">Refund (default)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Within 24 hours of booking, 48 hours or more before the start</td><td>95%</td></tr><tr><td>48 hours or more before the start</td><td>75%</td></tr><tr><td>24 to 48 hours before the start</td><td>50%</td></tr><tr><td>Under 24 hours, or after the start</td><td>0%</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-an-owner-s-page" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">An owner&#39;s page</h2><p class="gd-p">Open an owner from Owners. Three tabs: Overview, Terms and Invoices. <b class="gd-ui">Add another car</b> and <b class="gd-ui">New invoice</b> sit under the name.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The <b class="gd-ui">Onboarding checklist</b>, at the top: per car still onboarding, each step done, to do (with who it waits on: the owner, us, an Admin or the registry), blocked (with why) or not needed, and one button for the next thing to do. The owner and customer service see the same checklist.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Cars and terms: each car&#39;s Insurance Fee, Tracker Fee, management fee (Revenue Share), Install Fee and mode, with <b class="gd-ui">Edit</b> and History (see An owner&#39;s terms, car by car).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Onboarding photos</b>: the ownership permit, insurance slip and lender&#39;s permission of each car. <b class="gd-ui">Replace</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> (with a reason), <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Not accepted</b> (the owner reads why). A replaced photo that was approved is checked again. Every change is in the audit log.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Government forms</b>: the ServiceOntario forms each car needs, made by themselves when the terms are approved and again when a value changes, each with its status, what it misses, when it was made and its download. <b class="gd-ui">Make again</b> makes a car&#39;s forms anew now (a form signed in ink is kept); the values changed by hand stay, unless you tick <b class="gd-ui">Discard the values changed by hand</b>. Open a form and press <b class="gd-ui">Change a value</b> to correct one box of the official form before it is signed: choose the box, type the value and the reason. The form is made again as a new version; the earlier versions stay under <b class="gd-ui">Versions</b>, each with its download, and every change is in the audit log. <b class="gd-ui">Back to the records</b> puts a box&#39;s value from the records again. The owner always sees the current version only. Fleet can do the same. The owner signs each form on screen during onboarding. Beside the form, <b class="gd-ui">Owner&#39;s signature</b> shows the drawn signature (or typed name), who signed, when, from which IP address and device, and the version signed; the signature is never on the official form, and <b class="gd-ui">Download the print-ready form</b> has no signature. If you change a value after the owner signed, the form shows <b class="gd-ui">Changed since signed</b> with the boxes that changed, the owner gets one To do (the government forms step opens again) and one reminder email, and the earlier signature stays under <b class="gd-ui">Every signature</b>. The step is done when every form is signed.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Add cars from a list of VINs</b>: paste or upload the VINs, <b class="gd-ui">Preview</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Add</b>; a typo, a duplicate or a car already with us is reported, not added.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Upfront invoices: issue the first and last month amount agreed on each car&#39;s terms, for each car whose terms are set.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">Owner: address, sign-in and agreements; statements and payouts for this owner.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">8</span><div class="gd-t">Further down: <b class="gd-ui">View as (owner portal)</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Send password link</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Send a sign-in link to the owner portal</b>.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">A car&#39;s page has the same Government forms box (Owner &amp; documents).</p><div class="gd-figblock"><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/owners/50a834dc-270a-4c26-b79e-6396fa7bf2e1</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:410/1030"><img src="/guides/img/admin-13-owner-desktop-819a9f8b.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="410" height="1030"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:24.6%;top:4.4%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:16.1%;top:32.9%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:31.5%;top:73.2%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:21.2%;top:98.1%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-an-owner-s-terms-car-by-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">An owner&#39;s terms, car by car</h2><p class="gd-p">The table Cars and terms, at the top of an owner&#39;s page and its Terms tab: each car&#39;s Insurance Fee and Tracker Fee a month, management fee (Revenue Share), Install Fee and Management Mode, and since when they apply.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Edit</b> on a car&#39;s row. The row becomes fields: type the exact amounts (to the cent; the management fee in %). Before the Vehicle Schedule is signed you can also change the Install Fee, the Management Mode and the Onboarding Method.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Review</b>. It lists each value before and after, and what happens to each one. Nothing is saved yet.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Not signed yet (or not approved yet): <b class="gd-ui">Save</b> applies the numbers at once. An unsigned Vehicle Schedule is made again with them, so the owner signs these numbers; a car not approved yet keeps them for the Approve step.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Signed: a lower amount is in force from today, or the date you choose under Lower amounts from. No notice period is needed because it only lowers what the owner pays. A lower management fee does this while Settings &gt; Program, Lower management % without owner signature, is on (the default); off, the owner signs an updated Vehicle Schedule first.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Signed: a higher Insurance Fee or Tracker Fee needs 30 days&#39; written notice (Enrollment Agreement 4.8). Choose the date under Higher amounts from (30 days ahead at the earliest) and write the Reason: the owner reads it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Signed: a higher management fee (Revenue Share) needs the same notice and the owner&#39;s signature. The owner is emailed the notice and an updated Vehicle Schedule to sign; it applies from the date once signed, or from the day they sign if that is later. Higher fees in the same change apply from the date by the notice either way.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Confirm</b>. The owner is emailed the written notice, which is also a PDF in their portal and in the car&#39;s History.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">History, under each car, lists every period of terms (from, to, the amounts, and why: the Vehicle Schedule, a written notice, lowered) and every change with its notice. A change that has not started yet has Cancel (give the reason): the terms before it run on. An updated schedule waiting for the owner has Withdraw it; the owner signs it in the owner portal (never on paper). One change at a time: cancel or finish the one waiting before making the next.</p><p class="gd-p">The same editor is on the car&#39;s page (Records tab, Owner terms). The owner&#39;s default terms (for cars whose terms are set later) and the first and last month invoice stay on the Terms tab.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Invoices follow the dates: a month whose Insurance Fee or Tracker Fee changes part way is billed per day at each rate. The Revenue Share of a rental is the one in force on the day it is booked.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-pay-an-owner-a-flat-monthly-amount" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Pay an owner a flat monthly amount</h2><p class="gd-p">Some owners want the same amount every month for a car instead of a revenue share and fees. An Admin only, car by car.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the owner&#39;s Cars and terms table (or the car&#39;s page) and press <b class="gd-ui">Pay</b> on the car&#39;s row.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose <b class="gd-ui">Flat monthly payment</b>, type the <b class="gd-ui">Amount a month</b> (for example 900.00), the date under <b class="gd-ui">From</b> and, if it ends, the <b class="gd-ui">Last day</b>. Write the Reason (kept in the history).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Review</b>: it says what happens and lists any monthly invoice already issued for those days. Then press <b class="gd-ui">Confirm</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">From that date the owner&#39;s statement pays the amount every month (a part month by the day), with no revenue share and no Insurance Fee or Tracker Fee. Rentals ending on those days stay with CarmaCars, in the company figures.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Back to revenue share: press <b class="gd-ui">Pay</b>, choose Revenue share and the date. The flat period ends the day before; every period stays in the list.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A month already on an approved owner statement never changes: a new date starts after it. A monthly invoice already issued for flat days stays: void or credit it. A booking expense on a flat car is CarmaCars&#39; own unless you press <b class="gd-ui">Charge to the owner</b> beside it on the booking (an Admin only): it is then an owner cost on their statement. Owner costs recorded on the owner&#39;s account (tickets, tolls, damage of their own use) are charged as before.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-change-a-signed-car-s-management-mode" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Change a signed car&#39;s Management Mode</h2><p class="gd-p">Managed, Self-Managed or Turo-Only, from a date, for a car whose Vehicle Schedule is signed. An Admin only.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the owner&#39;s Cars and terms table (or the car&#39;s page) and press <b class="gd-ui">Change mode</b> on the car&#39;s row.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the <b class="gd-ui">New Management Mode</b> and its Onboarding Method (the options that fit how the car is held), the date under <b class="gd-ui">From</b>, and write the Reason: the owner reads it. Tick <b class="gd-ui">The owner asked for this</b> only when it is their own request.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Review</b>: it lists each value before and after (a Self-Managed car has no management fee; a Turo-Only car has no Fees and leaves the fleet insurance policy) and says whether the owner has to sign. Nothing is saved yet.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The owner asked and no amount goes up: no signature and no notice period. From today (or the date you chose) the car has the new mode, an updated Vehicle Schedule is issued with CarmaCars&#39; signature and the owner is emailed the notice.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Anything else (CarmaCars&#39; own decision, or a higher fee): the owner is emailed the notice and an updated Vehicle Schedule to sign, the date is at least 30 days away and the car stays as it is until it is signed. The owner signs it in the owner portal; in History, <b class="gd-ui">Withdraw it</b> if needed.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">A change dated ahead applies by itself on its date: the schedule is issued and the car moves. <b class="gd-ui">Cancel</b> in History (give the reason) stops it and emails the owner that their terms stay as they are. The same email goes when a notice of a higher fee is cancelled.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A shareholder-owned car has fixed terms. A car whose schedule is not signed yet changes its mode in the terms editor, where it applies at once.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-paid-and-signed" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Paid and signed</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owners</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Paid and signed</b> tab. What each owner still has to pay or sign, and how each item was done.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each owner shows how many items are open and how many are done. Owners with nothing left are hidden; press Show every owner to see them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Checklist and quick actions</b>. Each line says Signed in the portal, Signed on paper (before November 2026), Paid by e-Transfer, Not signed, and so on.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Paid by e-Transfer, cheque, cash or bank transfer? Press <b class="gd-ui">Record payment</b>. Choose Paid by, the Date received and the Reference (the cheque number for a cheque). Leave Amount empty for the full balance, or type less for a partial payment. Add a photo of the cheque or a screenshot if you have one.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Every agreement is signed in the owner portal: a signature on paper is not recorded. Only an official ServiceOntario form signed in ink is: press <b class="gd-ui">Record an official form signed in ink</b>, choose the form, check Signed by and Date signed, and upload the scan.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The same checklist sits at the top of each owner&#39;s page.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">You rarely need to come here: an upfront or overdue owner invoice is a line on To do with <b class="gd-ui">Record payment</b>, and an owner whose documents were sent two days ago or more and are not signed is a line with <b class="gd-ui">Waiting to sign</b> (open the owner to send the link again). Both pop-ups are the same forms, filled in.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">A recorded payment marks the invoice paid (or partly paid), stops the automatic debit for that amount, sends the owner a receipt, and shows &quot;Paid by e-Transfer on &quot; in their portal. An official form recorded as signed in ink counts as signed everywhere: the checklist, onboarding and the owner portal. The scan is kept privately with the owner&#39;s documents.</p><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>Recorded the wrong thing, or a cheque bounced? Press <b class="gd-ui">Void</b> beside it and give the reason. The invoice owes that amount again and the owner is told; a voided signature makes the item open again. Only an Admin can void.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-forms-c-and-d" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Forms C and D</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owner forms</b>. Forms C and D are signed on screen in the owner portal, with the witnesses on the same screen (one for Form C, two for Form D), and approved at once; Part 2 of Form D is signed for CarmaCars from the stored signatures (the signing officer, and the second signing officer of Program settings as CarmaCars&#39; witness). This queue holds only photos of paper copies sent before November 2026.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each row shows the owner, the form, the witnesses and when it was uploaded.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press Open to read the photo or scan. Check each marked spot is signed or initialled.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Send back</b> with What to fix (the owner reads this).</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/owner-forms</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/470"><img src="/guides/img/admin-22-owner-forms-desktop-c20ad300.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="470"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:29.2%;top:52.3%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:57.6%;top:52.3%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:76.7%;top:52.3%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-the-earnings-calculator-on-list-your-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The earnings calculator on List your car</h2><p class="gd-p">People who think of listing their car see what it could earn, near the top of List your car and, smaller, at the start of the application. Since release 48 the numbers are conservative and follow the season, and the result says plainly it is a rough estimate, not a promise.</p><p class="gd-p">They pick the year, make and model (or type the VIN), the <b class="gd-ui">days rented in an average month</b> (4 to 22, 12 at first) and their share (60% to 90%, 70% at first, &quot;set in your agreement&quot;). The page then works a whole year, month by month:</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>A month&#39;s rented days are the days chosen times that month&#39;s factor: summer runs above the average, winter under it, and the shoulder months (spring and fall) are the slowest.</li><li>A rented day earns the daily rate of cars like theirs on the site (the same make and model, else the class average, else the class&#39;s starting rate in Program settings) less a typical discount for weekly rates and offers.</li><li>Their share of that, less the monthly fees.</li></ul><p class="gd-p">It shows the average month, the year (the twelve months added up, never twelve of the best month), the range from the slowest month to the busiest, the rented days of each month as bars, and how many months the share would not cover the fees. &quot;Just cheaper insurance&quot; shows the fleet policy&#39;s fee and what they would keep in their slowest month.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>: <b class="gd-ui">Earnings calculator on List your car: the monthly insurance fee shown</b> and <b class="gd-ui">the monthly tracker fee shown</b>, in dollars a month.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Leave either one empty and the page says &quot;Insurance and tracker fees: quoted in your agreement&quot; and shows the earnings &quot;before fees&quot;. No amount is ever made up.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Set both and the page takes them off every month and the year. Each owner&#39;s real fees stay the ones in their agreement.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Earnings calculator on List your car: the rented days of an average month it starts from</b> (12): keep it low, a new car takes months to fill.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">The percent that comes off the listed daily rate on a rented day</b> (15).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">The factor of each month</b> (jan to dec) against an average month (1.00): by default June 1.10, July and August 1.30, December 0.85, January and February 0.75, May and September 0.85, March and October 0.70, April and November 0.65. Every month must be there.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-agreements-who-still-needs-to-sign" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Agreements: who still needs to sign</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Owners and partners</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owners</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Agreements</b>. Every owner with the agreements their deal needs, and where each one stands.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each owner shows their deal (revenue split, flat monthly or fleet lease) and one line per agreement: the Vehicle Enrollment Agreement, the Flat-Rate Vehicle Enrollment Agreement or the Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement, the Title-Holding and Lease Agreement, an Additional Vehicle Schedule for a car added later, the Partner agreement, and a Referral Override Agreement for each owner they referred.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Each line says <b class="gd-ui">Signed</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Sent, not signed</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Not sent</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Missing</b>. Missing means there is nothing to sign yet: set the terms of a car first, and the agreement is made from them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Send</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Send again</b>). The owner gets one email with the link to read and sign in their portal. An owner with no sign-in yet shows &quot;invite first&quot;: press Invite on the Owners list.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Owners whose agreements are all signed are hidden; press Show every owner to see them. The same lines are at the top of each owner&#39;s Terms tab.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>&quot;Awaiting lawyer OK&quot; marks the Referral Override Agreement until the lawyer approves its text (Program settings). The Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement is approved. Owners can sign either way.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-a-fleet-supplier-the-fleet-lease" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A fleet supplier: the fleet lease</h2><p class="gd-p">For a supplier&#39;s corporation that leases many cars to CarmaCars. Open the owner, <b class="gd-ui">Terms</b> tab, <b class="gd-ui">Fleet lease</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A supplier who signs up on the website as a fleet supplier (or whom staff add on the fleet supplier route) gets the default lease terms of Program settings and the default Upkeep Table at once: the card shows <b class="gd-ui">Fleet supplier route</b>. To agree other numbers, press <b class="gd-ui">Change the lease terms</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">A supplier on file without the route: press <b class="gd-ui">Enter the lease terms</b> and type what you agreed: the Regular Rate and the Troubled Rate (the lease a month for each car of that tier), the Claim Profit Share, the Early Write-Off Share, the Write-Off Period in months, the Later Write-Off Share and the Notice Period in days.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Check the <b class="gd-ui">Upkeep Table</b>: for each cost (engine, transmission, shocks, rustproofing, refurbishment, tires, brakes, oil changes, ball joints) the supplier or CarmaCars.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Add each car with <b class="gd-ui">Add another car</b> on the owner&#39;s page. The <b class="gd-ui">Fleet lease</b> step asks for the tier (Regular or Troubled) and the delivery date: the tier is required and set once. No fee or invoice step: the supplier pays CarmaCars nothing, and no owner invoice or debit is ever made for these cars.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">A car already on file: press <b class="gd-ui">Put on the lease</b> beside it, with the delivery date and the tier.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">The tier never changes. Typed the wrong one? Only an Admin can press <b class="gd-ui">Correct the tier</b>, with what was entered by mistake. It is corrected from the delivery (or from the day after the last approved statement) and kept in the audit log.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">The lease is paid in arrears on the 10th with the owner payouts: a car&#39;s first payment is on the first 10th at least one full month after its delivery and covers every month up to then. Part months are paid by the day; the statement line shows the calculation (rate, days, total).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">8</span><div class="gd-t">A claim on a leased car: settling it pays the supplier its Claim Profit Share of any profit, on its next statement. A write-off pays any lien first, then the supplier&#39;s Early or Later Write-Off Share of the balance by the months in service.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">9</span><div class="gd-t">An upkeep cost: <b class="gd-ui">Record an upkeep cost</b>. A cost the Upkeep Table gives the supplier comes off its next lease payment; one CarmaCars pays is not billed.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>New lease terms after the supplier signed wait for the supplier to sign the new agreement (it opens for signature at once). The cars keep the signed rates until then.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-approve-a-fleet-supplier-s-cars" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Approve a fleet supplier&#39;s cars</h2><p class="gd-p">A supplier who signed up on the website: his application is in <b class="gd-ui">Applications</b> like any other, with each car&#39;s VIN, plate and the tier he chose.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the application. Check the ownership copy of each car (he uploads it in his portal), the tier and who the car is registered to now. Its ServiceOntario forms were filled in when he added it: the lease (SR-LV-006 with his corporation as the registrant, SR-LV-012 with CarmaCars holding the plates) and, for a car not yet in his corporation, the transfer (ON00453 when the corporation has no RIN; 013-0169 and 013-1155 when an officer moves his own car in). A form still missing a value (a RIN, the odometer) shows what is missing, as on the other routes.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">A tier chosen by mistake: open the owner, <b class="gd-ui">Terms</b> tab, <b class="gd-ui">Fleet lease</b>, and press <b class="gd-ui">Correct the tier</b> beside the car, with what was chosen by mistake. Only an Admin can, and only before approval; it is kept in the audit log.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Approve: there are no terms or invoices to set. Check <b class="gd-ui">Delivered on</b> (the lease starts that day) and press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b>. Each car goes on the lease at its tier.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">He signs in the owner portal only: the Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement and the Title-Holding and Lease Agreement, and Form B on screen, with the full e-signature and its audit trail. Paper signatures cannot be recorded for him. Form D is in his packet and signed on screen with two witnesses; Form C is not asked.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement is final: the lawyer approved it, so it no longer shows &quot;Awaiting lawyer OK&quot;. The default lease terms are in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> (Fleet supplier route); a change there applies to suppliers who sign up later.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Owners &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Add an owner</b> offers the same route: choose <b class="gd-ui">A corporation</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Fleet supplier: leases the cars to CarmaCars</b>. So does <b class="gd-ui">Add a car for an owner</b> for a new owner.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-owner-rewards-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Owner rewards (release 48)</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owners</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owner rewards</b> shows the kits to ship, the upgrades to answer, each owner&#39;s months and code, and what the rewards cost.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">A merch kit to ship: when an owner presses Redeem on their Rewards tab, the kit shows here and on <b class="gd-ui">To do</b> with the address they confirmed. Ship it, then press <b class="gd-ui">Mark shipped</b> with the tracking number and what it cost. The owner is told and sees <b class="gd-ui">Shipped</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A free upgrade: when an owner&#39;s car is down for a repair they say CarmaCars caused, they ask here. <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b> with the amount CarmaCars covers (they get a one-time code), or <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b> with the reason they read.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Add a credit</b> gives an owner a credit by hand. Every credit is a line on the owner&#39;s next statement and an expense in the books (Owner rewards and credits, account 5310).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">What owners get: 20% off another car while theirs is out; a friends and family code (10% off a friend&#39;s first rental, and the owner earns the 20% kickback); $100 for referring an owner once the new car has been live 30 days; a merch kit at 6 months and a premium kit at 12; a $25 birthday rental credit; priority support and early access.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Every number is in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owner rewards</b>.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-sign-first-then-cars" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Sign first, then cars</h2><p class="gd-p">Program setting: Sign first (on). An owner&#39;s master agreement is made as soon as their profile is complete, with no car: the Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement with the Title-Holding and Lease Agreement for a fleet supplier, the Vehicle Enrollment Agreement otherwise. The owner signs it in the portal; CarmaCars countersigns at once with the signing officer of Settings.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Schedule A.</b> A supplier&#39;s car gets its numbered Schedule A entry when it is added (one at a time, or Add cars from a list of VINs with a tier and plate per row) and its government forms then. A program owner&#39;s car gets its entry when you set its terms. Cars added after the master is signed are confirmed by the owner with one signature per batch (the Additional Vehicle Schedule).</li><li><b class="gd-ui">The gate.</b> A car is not approved (a supplier&#39;s application), delivered (put on the lease) or rented (live) until the master agreement and its Schedule A entry are signed. Approving before the signature is kept: the application shows &quot;Approved, waiting for the signature&quot; and goes through by itself when the owner signs. If it cannot, you get a To do.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Agreements before cars.</b> The owner page and the application show exactly what is missing and who it waits on. Send reminder emails the owner (with the in-app notice and the push); once in 10 minutes at most.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Onboarding Method.</b> On the owner&#39;s Terms tab, Change the method corrects a car&#39;s method before its Vehicle Schedule is signed: the schedule, the plan and the government forms follow. The connector does the same with set_onboarding_method (previewed, then confirmed).</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Document check</b> (Owners &gt; Document check, and the connector&#39;s owner_documents_check): anything still inconsistent on an owner&#39;s documents, by owner, with what fixes it: a signing officer title that is a name (titles are roles, such as Director), a method that does not fit how the car is held (with none chosen, a car starts on Transfer, never Co-Registrant), a first and last month off the rule (two months of the Insurance Fee, which never carries HST), an empty value on a schedule.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Pickup not recorded.</b> A confirmed booking whose pickup was never recorded keeps its car presumed out after its return time: no new offer or booking goes on the car until you record the handover, the return or a no-show. Fleet gets the To do, then the Admins once the return time passed.</li><li>Onboarding steps, the owner pipeline: At the top of the owner page: each car&#39;s route (Transfer, Co-Registrant, Lease, Lease through a new Owner Corporation), every step done or not, and the current one with whose turn it is, its one action, what to bring, where to go, the expected time and the blockers. <b class="gd-ui">Advance this step</b> marks the current step done; <b class="gd-ui">Override a step</b> sets any step done, not needed, open again or back to the records. Both need a reason and are kept in the audit log. You get a To do when a step is yours (terms, listing); a step waiting 3 days (Program settings, owner_stage_stall_days) emails you. <b class="gd-ui">Marketing &gt; Owner pipeline</b> shows every car by step, with the nudge and the call script.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Incorporation referral</b> (Settings): owners who lease through a new corporation get Incorporate now with the provider&#39;s affiliate link. Off until you paste the link; each owner who opens it is listed with their code; mark Incorporated and Commission received from the provider&#39;s report.</li></ul></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('va', 'sales', 'chapter', 'fleet', 'You turn enquiries into bookings and owners into fleet: requests and offers, quotes for callers, and owner leads.

Your menu: To do, Today, My scorecard and My sales, then Requests and offers, Send an offer, Add a rental, New quote, Calendar and Buyer leads. The owners you bring in are on My sales.

## Requests, offers and new quotes

1. **Requests and offers**: the same queue customer service works, showing only what you can answer now. A request still with customer service is folded under "more not open to you yet", with the time it opens to you.
2. **Rentals** > **Bookings**: **My bookings**, every booking credited to you, offered by you or added by you, from the offer to the return, with its status, money and your commission (counting this month, waiting for approval, approved, paid).
3. **Send an offer**: one screen for a caller, sent at once, as in chapter 2. **New quote** still makes a request to offer later.
3. An offer that is out: **More actions** > **Edit the offer**, then **Send the update**.

![](/guides/img/va-sales-02-requests-desktop-2ab1d17d.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 580; address: carmacars.ca/va/requests; pins: 1 39.8 59.5")

> Tip: Your first reply target is 5 minutes, the "Quote sent" measure on your scorecard. Follow every offer out before it expires.

## Check the renter''s licence

Sales approve the renter''s licence like customer service: the licence front, the licence back and the selfie. The proof of coverage and the Protection Plan stay with customer service and Admins.

1. On **To do**, **Licences to check** lists each booking with an image waiting, the longest wait first. Press **Review the licence**.
2. On a booking, the card **Renter licence** has the same: press **Review the licence**.
3. Look at each image and each Flag line of the licence reader under the driver: no alteration, the selfie matches the licence photo.
4. One is wrong? Open **Reject this one** under it, type the reason the renter reads and press **Reject**. The renter is told and asked for a new image.
5. Then press **Approve all**: every image still waiting is approved at once. An image the system refuses is named with the reason.
6. To look again at an image already approved or rejected, press **View** beside it (it opens for one minute and the view is logged). After the 90-day removal it reads **Removed on** and the date.

> Tip: The booking history says who decided and the role, sales. Each opening of the images is logged and the links last one minute.

## In person or remote

Every Sales person works in one of two modes, on the same Sales screens. An Admin sets yours; it shows at the top of To do and on My sales.

|  | In person (Toronto) | Remote (anywhere) |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Commission | Under 50 rental days in the month 10%, from 50 days 15%, from 100 days 20% | Under 50 rental days 5%, from 50 days 10%, from 100 days 15% |
| Credit | Walk-ins, handovers you close, partner visits and the rentals you source | Only the rentals you source. A website request you answer with the first offer during one of your blocks counts as yours. Walk-ins and partner deals earn nothing |
| Hours | You choose | At least 20 hours a week of Thursday to Sunday afternoons (noon to 6 pm, Toronto time), replying within 15 minutes to the chats, texts and calls assigned to you |
| Every day | Nothing set | Marketplace and classified reposts, social media DM replies, three follow-ups on every quote, long-term and business outreach |
| Every month | Nothing set | 400 touches. Under 400 when the month ends, the month''s rate is one tier lower: 15% becomes 10%, 10% becomes 5%, 5% becomes 2.5% |

## Remote: your duties

On **To do**, **Remote duties** shows this month''s touches against 400, today''s checklist, the peak hours you scheduled this week and your reply time.

1. Most touches count by themselves: an offer you send, a message or text you send from the portal, a live chat you answer (once a day for each chat), a call or text from the phone line, an ad you post, a call or message to a car owner.
2. For anything else press **Log a touch**: choose the type and add the link of the post, profile or listing if there is one.
3. The checklist ticks itself as the day''s touches come in. Three follow-ups on every quote stays open while a deal of yours has fewer than three.
4. Under My availability choose this week or next, press **Add a block** for each time you will be on, then **Save the week**. Days already past stay as they were.
5. A website request you answer with the first offer during a block is credited to you as sourced, even if you chose Entered for CarmaCars. Off your blocks it stays a claim for an Admin.

> Tip: An Admin can void a touch logged by mistake. Once an Admin approves a month, its mode, its rates and its touches no longer change; a refund can still lower the tier, as for everyone.

## My sales

Open **Me**, the **My sales** tab. It shows your own sales and commissions only.

1. Commissions comes first. Your rate depends on your mode and the rental days of the month: in person 10%, 15% from 50 days, 20% from 100; remote 5%, 10% and 15%. The bar shows your days against the target of 100, and says when your rate rises. By month gives each month in one line: the mode, the days, the rate and, for remote, the touches and any drop.
2. The tiles show this week: quotes created, offers sent, rentals added, bookings confirmed, conversion, booked revenue and follow-ups due. Press **By month** for months, **By week** for weeks.
3. By week (or By month) lists each period with the same figures, newest first.
4. Follow-ups due lists your open deals with what to do next: send the offer, follow up before the offer expires, or follow up while the renter signs and pays. Red means it is past due.
5. Deals lists every booking you created, added or sent an offer on in the last 180 days, with its status and what it counts. Open a request, an offer or a rental you added from its number.

| Figure | How it is counted |
| --- | --- |
| Credited to you | A quote you created, a rental you added, or a website request whose first offer you sent. An Admin can give a deal to someone else. |
| Quotes created, offers sent, rentals added | Counted on the day they happened. |
| Bookings confirmed, booked revenue | Counted on the day the booking was confirmed. |
| Conversion | Of the deals credited to you in the period, the share confirmed so far. |
| Booked revenue | The rental charge before tax, after discounts. A cancelled booking counts only what was kept; refunds come off. |
| Rental days (Sales) | The days of the completed, paid rentals you sourced that end in the month. The month''s tier applies to all of that month''s rentals. |

> Tip: Sales commissions are approved after the month ends, when the month''s tier is known. A refund that drops the month under a tier lowers every commission of that month; anything already paid comes off your next payment.

## Owners you bring in

Bring in car owners on **My work** > **My sales**, card **Owners you bring in**. Every owner you bring in is credited to you as "sourced by", with their cars. Only an Admin can change that later.

1. **Invite an owner**: enter their name, email and phone, tick **The owner asked me to send it**, then press **Send the invitation**. They get an email with your link to apply.
2. **Copy my owner link**: your own link to the application, for a message or a post. Anyone who applies with it is credited to you.
3. **Start an application**: you fill in the owner and the car for them, with **Take a photo** (or **Choose a photo**) of the ownership permit to fill in the car. It goes to an Admin as an application to approve. The terms and invoices are the Admin''s. A corporation that leases its cars to CarmaCars: choose **A corporation**, then Route **Fleet supplier: leases the cars to CarmaCars**, and each car''s tier (**Regular** or **Troubled**). A fleet supplier can also apply himself from `carmacars.ca/list-your-car`: your owner link works for it too.
4. The row of five figures follows your owners: **Invited**, **Applied**, **Approved**, **Car live** and **First paid rental**. Below, each owner shows their stage and their cars.

5. Someone who starts the application on the website and stops for 30 minutes comes to you: a task "Unfinished owner application" and their row on My sales (Lead). Call or text them; the follow-up emails go by themselves until they finish.

> Tip: An owner already on file, or invited first by another salesperson, cannot be invited again. Ask an Admin if you brought them in.

## Ask for your commission on an owner

There is no set amount. For each owner you bring in, you ask for one, and an Admin decides.

1. On the owner''s row press **Ask for a commission**.
2. Choose **A flat amount** and type it, or **A percent**: type the percent, choose what it is of (the company''s share of their cars'' rentals, or their cars'' rental revenue) and for how long (a number of months, or as long as the car is with us).
3. Add a note for the Admin if you like, then press **Send to an Admin**.
4. While it waits you can press **Change my request**. Once an Admin approves, changes or declines it, the row says so, with their note.

| Approved as | When it is earned |
| --- | --- |
| A flat amount | Once, at the owner''s first paid rental: the first completed rental of any of their cars, paid in full |
| A percent | On each completed, paid rental of their cars that ends after the approval, from the month of the first one, for the months approved |

> Tip: Nothing is earned before an Admin approves the request, and nothing on CarmaCars'' own cars, a partner''s, a shareholder''s or your own. Each commission then goes through the usual steps on My sales: pending approval, approved, paid.

## Buyer leads

1. **Buyer leads**: each request from the /buy pages, with the car, budget and timing.
2. Press **Take it** to make it yours, then call them.
3. Press **Update** to set the status. When you close a lead, say why.

> Tip: Owner leads are not here. The owners you invite or add are on **My sales**, **Owners you bring in**, and you see only your own. Customer service works the full owner pipeline.

An offer that has been expired for 7 days leaves Requests and offers and becomes a renter lead: you get the To do "Expired offer: win the renter back" (the lead goes to the Sales person with the fewest open leads) with the renter''s contact, the car and the dates they wanted. Call or text them, then mark the lead contacted or closed.

**Reopen offer** on an expired booking (or the **Expired** filter of Requests) sends the offer again in one click, open 12 hours (never past 1 hour before the pickup) unless you set the hours; a pickup time that has passed asks for new dates first. "Renter wants expired offer reopened" To dos come from the renter''s own button. The offer screens block **Send** with **Pickup time has passed: update it** until the pickup is moved.

## Book it now (release 33)
When you send an offer, tick **Book it now (no renter approval)** when the renter has already agreed. The offer goes out and an Admin approves it in one tap: the booking then waits for payment, the car is held, and the renter gets one link to sign and pay. You can also have them sign and pay with you: open the booking, **Sign now on this device**, then take the card on this device.
Already sent the offer? Ask the assistant: "Book the offer of CC-10482 now, the customer agreed by phone". It shows a card; **Confirm** sends the same request to an Admin, who approves in one tap.

## When a check stops the pickup or the return (release 33)
On the booking page, **What stops the pickup now** (or the return) lists each check that stops it, in plain words. When the trip must go ahead anyway, press **Ask an Admin to override the pickup** (or the return), give the actual time, the km and fuel if you know them, and why. An Admin gets an alert and approves in one tap; the pickup (or the return) is then recorded with the time you entered, and the booking''s history says who asked and who approved. You can cancel your request while it waits. A trip that happened and was never recorded: **Ask to record a past trip** with both times; once an Admin approves, the booking lands in Returned so the deposit can be settled.

## Leads and claims

Open **Leads**. Every lead is there: renter leads (forms, live chat, the phone number box, games, expired offers, requests not sent, missed calls, Live visitors), owner leads and partner leads, new and hot first. A new-lead alert on your phone opens that lead.

1. Press **Next lead**, or **Claim** on a card. The lead is yours for 15 minutes.
2. Press **Call**, **Text** or **Email**: your phone or mail app opens and the contact is logged. Each contact (or **Note**) adds 15 minutes, up to 60 minutes from your claim.
3. Press **Outcome**: Contacted, Call booked, Applied, Won or Lost (say why). Or **Mark handled** when there is nothing more to do.
4. Can''t finish? Press **Unclaim** so someone else can take it. A claim that runs out goes back to the pool by itself.

You hold at most 25 leads at once. Your numbers are on To do under **My leads**: leads claimed, won, close rate (won out of claimed), contacted, time to first contact and claims that ran out, today, this week and this month. Owner leads are also under **Owners** > **Leads**.

## The person behind the lead (release 40)

Press **The person** on a lead card, or open the lead, to see everything we know about them in one place: their name and the name they go by, phone and email, account and whether the licence is verified (yes or no, never the number), every booking with the car, dates, status, total and anything owed, the deposit, open requests and offers sent, their earlier leads, messages, calls and texts, notes, reviews, incidents, and who has handled them. **Signals** lists everything they did with us, newest first: calls and texts, WhatsApp, chat, emails, visits, cars and offers looked at, bookings and reviews. The intent score counts all of it.

When the renter is outside your window, you see their contact and account until the lead is yours: claim it (or an Admin assigns it to you) and the rest opens, logged as a record you opened for a reason. An Admin can assign leads to you in bulk: they show **Assigned to you by an Admin**, do not run out, and do not count against your limit of open leads.
## Call minutes (release 35)
Your home shows **My call minutes**: today, this week and this month, for connected calls made with the site''s **Call** button. Customer numbers are hidden for Sales; call and text with the buttons on the page.


## Get a renter ready for the pickup (release 35)
Your work does not stop at the offer. Until the car is handed over you can do everything that gets the renter good to go:
- **Payment**: send a pay link or a deposit link on Money (text or email), or take the card on this device, also on a confirmed booking.
- **The offer**: edit it, send it again with a later expiry, withdraw it or record that the renter approved by phone, also while it waits for payment.
- **ID and coverage**: approve or reject the licence, the selfie and the proof of coverage, with the reason the renter sees.
- **Drivers and agreement**: send each additional driver their signing link, or the agreement again.
- **Name change asked for**: when a verified renter asks for a name or date of birth correction, it shows on the booking; check it against the licence, then **Approve** or **Decline**.

The booking page shows **Ready for the rental**: one line for each thing the pickup needs (offer accepted, paid, licence and selfie, coverage, deposit, drivers, agreement, add-ons in the car), green when done, with what to press when not. Refunds, cancellations, deposit releases and removing a paid add-on stay with customer service, Finance and Admins.

## The Prepare checklist (release 35)
On a booking with add-ons, **Prepare for the pickup** shows each add-on with its quantity, ticked or not by field staff, who ticked it and when, and the pickup or delivery job with its field person. It is on the booking and on the car page, for Sales, customer service, Fleet and Finance.

## Rebooking, intent and offers (release 35)

- A returning renter''s new request comes straight to you when you had their last booking, with the usual claim time.
- Each lead shows its intent (hot, warm or cold) and what the person said they want, read from calls with their transcripts, texts, emails, chat and visits. Call hot leads first.
- Offers are three steps: car and dates, price, review and send. Every version is kept; you can load an old one as a new offer.
- Prices stay between the owner''s daily minimum and maximum; only an Admin allows one outside them.
- Verified renters with the Gold Rewards tier or above can book instantly; their booking is marked Instant (repeat renter).
- Rewards: tell renters they earn points for a photo with their review and every rental after the first.

## Calls first, texts after (release 37)

Your main priority is always to be on the phone with people.

1. Answer a ringing call before anything else, and return a missed call at once.
2. **Call before you text.** On a lead, a renter or a booking, **Call** is the first button and **Text** the second.
3. A text is a follow-up: after a call attempt (no answer, a voicemail left), or when the person asked for a text.
4. On your To do and on **Unanswered**, missed calls and call-backs are listed above unanswered texts.

## A lead customer service is handling (release 37)

When customer service or Fleet are on a call with a lead, the lead and the lists say **Being handled by** their first name, their function and the time. Leave it alone: you cannot claim it, call, text or email it, or set an outcome, and **Next lead** skips it. When their time ends, the lead returns to you if you had a claim on it or brought it, else to the open list. The booking credit rules do not change.

## Check-in and check-out on one screen (release 42)

**Start the check-in (pickup)** and **Start the check-out (return)** on the booking, and **Check in** or **Check out** on the To do list, open the same screen field staff use, made for a phone held in one hand:

1. Every part is on one page in the order you do it, with a green tick once it is complete: the ready check, the renter, licence and card (one tap each), the odometer, fuel and keys, the photos, damage, the tracker, then the signatures.
2. What is known is filled in: the odometer and fuel from the Tracker when it reported in the last 30 minutes (else from the car''s last report), the keys, and Standard for the cleanliness of a return. Check each against the car and change what differs.
3. Photos are one tap each: **Take this photo** always shows the next angle.
4. What is optional is folded away: new damage, a note, belongings, a renter who is not there or will not sign.
5. The button at the bottom says what is still needed (for example "Next: Odometer") and takes you to it. When everything is in, press **Hand over the keys** or **Complete the return**.

Nothing was dropped: the condition report still needs every photo, the readings and the signatures, and the database refuses a handover with anything missing. Leave the page and come back: your answers and photos are still there.

**Check in with photos already taken (from the gallery)** is still under the button, for a car that was photographed earlier.

## A late return is a choice (release 42)

A car that comes back after the grace period is never charged by itself. The booking shows **Late return** with how late the car was and five choices, each with what it costs:

1. **Charge as an extension**: every started day late at the booking''s daily rate, as an extension would have cost.
2. **Charge extra days**: you choose the days, from 1 up to the started days, at the daily rate.
3. **Charge the late return fee**: the fee of the rental terms (whole days at the daily rate, the started hours after them at the hourly fee, capped a day).
4. **Charge a custom amount**: type the amount before tax and what it is for. The renter sees the reason.
5. **Waive it**: no charge, with the reason.

Press **Save the late return charge**. The charge goes on the return statement and is taken as every return charge is: from the deposit, then the card on file, then a pay link. The renter gets a message on the booking that says what was chosen, and the booking history keeps who chose and why.

Until someone chooses, nothing is charged for the late return and Fleet has the To do "Late return: choose the charge". Field staff can choose on the return screen as they complete the return.

> Good to know: A custom amount above your single limit, and a waiver by anyone other than an Admin, Finance or Fleet, waits for an Admin: they get the To do "Late return: approve the charge" and press **Approve as asked**, or choose another way. Only an Admin changes a late return that is already decided, and not once it is on a statement or paid.

## A request that did not go through (release 42)

A **Request did not go through** To-do means a customer pressed Send request and it was refused or failed. The To-do has their name, email, phone, the car, the dates and the reason they were shown.

1. Call or text them soon: they wanted to book.
2. Their answers are still in the form on their device. Tell them what to change (the reason says which field), or make the offer yourself with **New quote**.
3. When their request arrives, the To-do closes by itself. If they no longer want the car, complete it with a note.

An urgent one means our system could not take the request: the customer was told we will contact them, so contact them first.

## A lead''s phone number (release 46)

Customer numbers show with dots in place of most digits. **Call** and **Text** still reach the person through the business number.

1. Need the whole number of one lead (to give it at the counter or to dial it yourself)? On the lead, press **Ask an Admin to show the number**. An Admin gets a To do on that lead; asking again adds no second one.
2. When an Admin shows it to you, the lead says **Number shown by an Admin**: the full number, with a call link and **Copy**, on that lead only: its page, its card in the list and its calls. You also get an alert that opens the lead. Every other lead stays hidden, except the same number where it belongs to the same person (their renter record or another lead with that phone).
3. If the lead goes to another salesperson, the number is hidden from you again by itself, and the new salesperson sees it hidden until an Admin shows it to them.

## Where a lead came from (release 48)

Every lead card and every lead''s page says where the person came from, for forms and requests sent from the website.

1. On a lead card, the badge under the source reads for example "ChatGPT", "Google search", "Google Ads", "Perplexity", "Bing" or "Direct (typed or bookmarked)", with the search terms when we have them and "First page" (the first page they opened on the site).
2. On the lead''s page, the card **Where they came from** lists: **Came from**, **Search terms**, **First page they opened**, **Page of the latest visit**, **Referring page** and **Campaign**. A row we do not know is left out.
3. Search terms come from the ad or campaign link, or from the search page they came from (Bing and DuckDuckGo sometimes send them). Google does not send the words searched: for a Google visit the card lists the top Google searches that bring people to that first page, from Search Console.
4. Use it in the first call: someone who came from "kill switch for car" wants the tracker; someone who landed on a monthly rental page wants a monthly price.

> Good to know: a call, a chat and a lead typed by staff have no source, and the card says so. Leads from before release 48 have none either.

## Duplicate leads (release 48)

The same person often writes twice: the contact form, then the chat, then a call. Your lead list keeps them as one, so two people never call the same person.

1. A new website form from someone who already has an open lead of the same kind (same email or same phone, in the last 14 days) joins that lead by itself. Its message shows on the older lead under "Also wrote", marked "merged automatically".
2. A lead with another lead of the same person shows "possible duplicate: merge" on its card. Open it: the card "Possible duplicates" lists each one with why it matches (same email, same phone, same browser).
3. Press **Merge**. The oldest lead is kept. The other''s message, calls, texts, chats and notes move to it, and the other is closed as merged. Nothing is deleted.
4. **Merge all into the oldest** does every duplicate at once.
5. Two people who share an email or a phone (a couple, an office line): press **Different person**. The pair is never suggested again.
6. A renter lead and an owner lead of the same person stay apart: they are different conversations.

> Good to know: a lead that was already handled is not reopened by a new form. The new form is a new lead, with the merge offered, so you decide.

## Renter sent an e-Transfer (release 49)

You cannot record a payment; Finance does. When a renter says they sent the e-Transfer on a booking waiting for payment:

1. Open the booking, the **Money** tab, then **Renter sent an e-Transfer**.
2. Type the amount sent, choose what it covers (**The rental and fees**, **The deposit** or **Both**), the sender''s name if you have it, and add the screenshot or proof (a photo or a PDF). **Send to Finance**.
3. Nothing is marked paid. The booking shows **e-Transfer reported, waiting for Finance** and Finance gets a Check e-Transfer To do.
4. You are told when Finance answers: confirmed (the payment is recorded and the booking confirmed), or not received with their reason. Then check with the renter and report it again.
5. One report waits at a time on a booking.
', 'Sales', 'Requests and offers, new quotes and owner leads.',
  'You turn enquiries into bookings and owners into fleet: requests and offers, quotes for callers, and owner leads.

Your menu: To do, Today, My scorecard and My sales, then Requests and offers, Send an offer, Add a rental, New quote, Calendar and Buyer leads. The owners you bring in are on My sales.

## Requests, offers and new quotes

1. **Requests and offers**: the same queue customer service works, showing only what you can answer now. A request still with customer service is folded under "more not open to you yet", with the time it opens to you.
2. **Rentals** > **Bookings**: **My bookings**, every booking credited to you, offered by you or added by you, from the offer to the return, with its status, money and your commission (counting this month, waiting for approval, approved, paid).
3. **Send an offer**: one screen for a caller, sent at once, as in chapter 2. **New quote** still makes a request to offer later.
3. An offer that is out: **More actions** > **Edit the offer**, then **Send the update**.

![](/guides/img/va-sales-02-requests-desktop-2ab1d17d.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 580; address: carmacars.ca/va/requests; pins: 1 39.8 59.5")

> Tip: Your first reply target is 5 minutes, the "Quote sent" measure on your scorecard. Follow every offer out before it expires.

## Check the renter''s licence

Sales approve the renter''s licence like customer service: the licence front, the licence back and the selfie. The proof of coverage and the Protection Plan stay with customer service and Admins.

1. On **To do**, **Licences to check** lists each booking with an image waiting, the longest wait first. Press **Review the licence**.
2. On a booking, the card **Renter licence** has the same: press **Review the licence**.
3. Look at each image and each Flag line of the licence reader under the driver: no alteration, the selfie matches the licence photo.
4. One is wrong? Open **Reject this one** under it, type the reason the renter reads and press **Reject**. The renter is told and asked for a new image.
5. Then press **Approve all**: every image still waiting is approved at once. An image the system refuses is named with the reason.
6. To look again at an image already approved or rejected, press **View** beside it (it opens for one minute and the view is logged). After the 90-day removal it reads **Removed on** and the date.

> Tip: The booking history says who decided and the role, sales. Each opening of the images is logged and the links last one minute.

## In person or remote

Every Sales person works in one of two modes, on the same Sales screens. An Admin sets yours; it shows at the top of To do and on My sales.

|  | In person (Toronto) | Remote (anywhere) |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Commission | Under 50 rental days in the month 10%, from 50 days 15%, from 100 days 20% | Under 50 rental days 5%, from 50 days 10%, from 100 days 15% |
| Credit | Walk-ins, handovers you close, partner visits and the rentals you source | Only the rentals you source. A website request you answer with the first offer during one of your blocks counts as yours. Walk-ins and partner deals earn nothing |
| Hours | You choose | At least 20 hours a week of Thursday to Sunday afternoons (noon to 6 pm, Toronto time), replying within 15 minutes to the chats, texts and calls assigned to you |
| Every day | Nothing set | Marketplace and classified reposts, social media DM replies, three follow-ups on every quote, long-term and business outreach |
| Every month | Nothing set | 400 touches. Under 400 when the month ends, the month''s rate is one tier lower: 15% becomes 10%, 10% becomes 5%, 5% becomes 2.5% |

## Remote: your duties

On **To do**, **Remote duties** shows this month''s touches against 400, today''s checklist, the peak hours you scheduled this week and your reply time.

1. Most touches count by themselves: an offer you send, a message or text you send from the portal, a live chat you answer (once a day for each chat), a call or text from the phone line, an ad you post, a call or message to a car owner.
2. For anything else press **Log a touch**: choose the type and add the link of the post, profile or listing if there is one.
3. The checklist ticks itself as the day''s touches come in. Three follow-ups on every quote stays open while a deal of yours has fewer than three.
4. Under My availability choose this week or next, press **Add a block** for each time you will be on, then **Save the week**. Days already past stay as they were.
5. A website request you answer with the first offer during a block is credited to you as sourced, even if you chose Entered for CarmaCars. Off your blocks it stays a claim for an Admin.

> Tip: An Admin can void a touch logged by mistake. Once an Admin approves a month, its mode, its rates and its touches no longer change; a refund can still lower the tier, as for everyone.

## My sales

Open **Me**, the **My sales** tab. It shows your own sales and commissions only.

1. Commissions comes first. Your rate depends on your mode and the rental days of the month: in person 10%, 15% from 50 days, 20% from 100; remote 5%, 10% and 15%. The bar shows your days against the target of 100, and says when your rate rises. By month gives each month in one line: the mode, the days, the rate and, for remote, the touches and any drop.
2. The tiles show this week: quotes created, offers sent, rentals added, bookings confirmed, conversion, booked revenue and follow-ups due. Press **By month** for months, **By week** for weeks.
3. By week (or By month) lists each period with the same figures, newest first.
4. Follow-ups due lists your open deals with what to do next: send the offer, follow up before the offer expires, or follow up while the renter signs and pays. Red means it is past due.
5. Deals lists every booking you created, added or sent an offer on in the last 180 days, with its status and what it counts. Open a request, an offer or a rental you added from its number.

| Figure | How it is counted |
| --- | --- |
| Credited to you | A quote you created, a rental you added, or a website request whose first offer you sent. An Admin can give a deal to someone else. |
| Quotes created, offers sent, rentals added | Counted on the day they happened. |
| Bookings confirmed, booked revenue | Counted on the day the booking was confirmed. |
| Conversion | Of the deals credited to you in the period, the share confirmed so far. |
| Booked revenue | The rental charge before tax, after discounts. A cancelled booking counts only what was kept; refunds come off. |
| Rental days (Sales) | The days of the completed, paid rentals you sourced that end in the month. The month''s tier applies to all of that month''s rentals. |

> Tip: Sales commissions are approved after the month ends, when the month''s tier is known. A refund that drops the month under a tier lowers every commission of that month; anything already paid comes off your next payment.

## Owners you bring in

Bring in car owners on **My work** > **My sales**, card **Owners you bring in**. Every owner you bring in is credited to you as "sourced by", with their cars. Only an Admin can change that later.

1. **Invite an owner**: enter their name, email and phone, tick **The owner asked me to send it**, then press **Send the invitation**. They get an email with your link to apply.
2. **Copy my owner link**: your own link to the application, for a message or a post. Anyone who applies with it is credited to you.
3. **Start an application**: you fill in the owner and the car for them, with **Take a photo** (or **Choose a photo**) of the ownership permit to fill in the car. It goes to an Admin as an application to approve. The terms and invoices are the Admin''s. A corporation that leases its cars to CarmaCars: choose **A corporation**, then Route **Fleet supplier: leases the cars to CarmaCars**, and each car''s tier (**Regular** or **Troubled**). A fleet supplier can also apply himself from `carmacars.ca/list-your-car`: your owner link works for it too.
4. The row of five figures follows your owners: **Invited**, **Applied**, **Approved**, **Car live** and **First paid rental**. Below, each owner shows their stage and their cars.

5. Someone who starts the application on the website and stops for 30 minutes comes to you: a task "Unfinished owner application" and their row on My sales (Lead). Call or text them; the follow-up emails go by themselves until they finish.

> Tip: An owner already on file, or invited first by another salesperson, cannot be invited again. Ask an Admin if you brought them in.

## Ask for your commission on an owner

There is no set amount. For each owner you bring in, you ask for one, and an Admin decides.

1. On the owner''s row press **Ask for a commission**.
2. Choose **A flat amount** and type it, or **A percent**: type the percent, choose what it is of (the company''s share of their cars'' rentals, or their cars'' rental revenue) and for how long (a number of months, or as long as the car is with us).
3. Add a note for the Admin if you like, then press **Send to an Admin**.
4. While it waits you can press **Change my request**. Once an Admin approves, changes or declines it, the row says so, with their note.

| Approved as | When it is earned |
| --- | --- |
| A flat amount | Once, at the owner''s first paid rental: the first completed rental of any of their cars, paid in full |
| A percent | On each completed, paid rental of their cars that ends after the approval, from the month of the first one, for the months approved |

> Tip: Nothing is earned before an Admin approves the request, and nothing on CarmaCars'' own cars, a partner''s, a shareholder''s or your own. Each commission then goes through the usual steps on My sales: pending approval, approved, paid.

## Buyer leads

1. **Buyer leads**: each request from the /buy pages, with the car, budget and timing.
2. Press **Take it** to make it yours, then call them.
3. Press **Update** to set the status. When you close a lead, say why.

> Tip: Owner leads are not here. The owners you invite or add are on **My sales**, **Owners you bring in**, and you see only your own. Customer service works the full owner pipeline.

An offer that has been expired for 7 days leaves Requests and offers and becomes a renter lead: you get the To do "Expired offer: win the renter back" (the lead goes to the Sales person with the fewest open leads) with the renter''s contact, the car and the dates they wanted. Call or text them, then mark the lead contacted or closed.

**Reopen offer** on an expired booking (or the **Expired** filter of Requests) sends the offer again in one click, open 12 hours (never past 1 hour before the pickup) unless you set the hours; a pickup time that has passed asks for new dates first. "Renter wants expired offer reopened" To dos come from the renter''s own button. The offer screens block **Send** with **Pickup time has passed: update it** until the pickup is moved.

